258
00:08:47,942 --> 00:08:51,942
Some people "hijack" mountains.

259
00:08:52,742 --> 00:08:55,312
- Hijacking is like... - That's...

260
00:08:55,382 --> 00:08:56,852
Hijacking is seizing vehicles.

261
00:08:57,082 --> 00:08:58,552
- Dowoon isn't good at English. - Really?

262
00:08:58,552 --> 00:08:59,722
- He is. - Is that so?

263
00:08:59,722 --> 00:09:02,022
- Do you mean trail running? - I see.

264
00:09:02,892 --> 00:09:04,692
- Have you tried that? - Yes, I have.

265
00:09:04,692 --> 00:09:06,462
- My gosh. - I can tackle small mountains.

266
00:09:06,462 --> 00:09:07,732
I can run up about 5km.

267
00:09:08,232 --> 00:09:10,002
It's really fun.

268
00:09:10,462 --> 00:09:12,362
- By the way... - Did Hyun Moo tell you...

269
00:09:12,362 --> 00:09:15,602
when he would be here? Did he tell you that?

270
00:09:15,602 --> 00:09:17,042
He only told me to show up.

271
00:09:18,172 --> 00:09:19,942
(Quiet)

272
00:09:19,942 --> 00:09:21,312
I think he's late.

273
00:09:21,772 --> 00:09:22,882
He's just late.

274
00:09:23,542 --> 00:09:25,242
He won't say he can't make it, right?

275
00:09:25,242 --> 00:09:26,312
(Feeling guilty)

276
00:09:26,312 --> 00:09:29,922
- But that won't be so bad. - I agree. It'll still be fun.

277
00:09:29,922 --> 00:09:32,222
- We can... - What if they run without him?

278
00:09:33,422 --> 00:09:35,222
I really want to run. It's driving me crazy.

279
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:37,222
This is crazy.

280
00:09:37,222 --> 00:09:38,222
(A crazy urge to run)

281
00:09:38,222 --> 00:09:39,362
This feels great.

282
00:09:40,362 --> 00:09:41,832
(Guys, give me a bit more time.)

283
00:09:42,392 --> 00:09:44,202
(Sucking)

284
00:09:45,762 --> 00:09:47,002
Oh, I hate this!

285
00:09:48,202 --> 00:09:49,272
The air feels so fresh.

286
00:09:49,272 --> 00:09:51,842
(The crew chief of the Fun Run is running to them.)

287
00:09:51,842 --> 00:09:54,842
My gosh, look at these stairs. I should walk up.

288
00:09:55,312 --> 00:09:56,842
Climbing the stairs isn't fun.

289
00:09:58,112 --> 00:10:00,112
Darn it. Why did I ask to meet them here?

290
00:10:01,712 --> 00:10:02,752
Look at him.

291
00:10:02,752 --> 00:10:03,822
(Panting)

292
00:10:03,922 --> 00:10:05,052
There were so many stairs.

293
00:10:05,352 --> 00:10:08,052
Is drinking water a mission or something? This is...

294
00:10:08,492 --> 00:10:09,862
This isn't good. I'm already tired.

295
00:10:09,862 --> 00:10:12,222
(This isn't good. I'm already tired.)

296
00:10:12,932 --> 00:10:13,932
(Huddled up)

297
00:10:13,932 --> 00:10:15,032
That's interesting.

298
00:10:15,432 --> 00:10:16,932
- The next-closest one? - Yes.

299
00:10:16,932 --> 00:10:18,002
You should speak casually to us.

300
00:10:18,002 --> 00:10:19,672
- You should drop the honorifics. - You should drop the honorifics.

301
00:10:19,672 --> 00:10:21,302
- Should I do that? - Yes, please.

302
00:10:21,302 --> 00:10:22,702
Let's do that then. Nice to meet you.

303
00:10:22,902 --> 00:10:24,942
- Great. - Nice to meet you.

304
00:10:25,172 --> 00:10:28,272
Will we need sunglasses later when we start running?

305
00:10:28,772 --> 00:10:29,812
I...

306
00:10:29,812 --> 00:10:31,212
- I can drop the honorifics now. - Yes.

307
00:10:31,212 --> 00:10:33,152
When you're running,

308
00:10:33,452 --> 00:10:35,352
- the wind might blow against you. - I see.

309
00:10:36,112 --> 00:10:37,682
Dust can go into your eyes.

310
00:10:37,682 --> 00:10:39,652
- They didn't know I was there. - So...

311
00:10:39,952 --> 00:10:41,452
I brought my sunglasses.

312
00:10:42,092 --> 00:10:43,862
- I came well-prepared. - My gosh. What?

313
00:10:44,392 --> 00:10:45,722
- I see. - My gosh. What?

314
00:10:46,022 --> 00:10:47,162
- I see. - Gosh.

315
00:10:47,432 --> 00:10:51,132
(They finally spot the crew chief.)

316
00:10:53,572 --> 00:10:54,602
I thought he was going to fall.

317
00:10:54,602 --> 00:10:55,772
- Are you that happy to see me? - Hello.

318
00:10:55,772 --> 00:10:57,842
It looks like you guys are getting along.

319
00:10:57,942 --> 00:11:01,842
I thought you guys might feel awkward with each other.

320
00:11:01,842 --> 00:11:04,712
Gosh, Hyun Moo. Are you wearing makeup?

321
00:11:06,612 --> 00:11:09,012
I've never seen anyone wear makeup when they go for a run.

322
00:11:09,012 --> 00:11:10,852
- That's the Fun Run. - My gosh. I hate it.

323
00:11:11,182 --> 00:11:12,992
You sort of look like a cotton swab. You know?

324
00:11:13,452 --> 00:11:15,922
Your face is white, but your neck is brown.

325
00:11:15,922 --> 00:11:17,092
(White and dark)

326
00:11:17,262 --> 00:11:19,632
I had to put on some makeup since I was running with you guys.

327
00:11:19,992 --> 00:11:21,792
- You didn't? - We didn't.

328
00:11:22,732 --> 00:11:24,132
- Sit down. - Okay.

329
00:11:24,132 --> 00:11:26,432
- The white cast is very noticeable. - It is?

330
00:11:27,602 --> 00:11:30,902
The Fun Run will open up a new horizon in the running scene.

331
00:11:31,372 --> 00:11:33,342
To hold the inauguration ceremony for the first batch...

332
00:11:33,572 --> 00:11:34,972
You're so good at taking all the credit.

333
00:11:36,682 --> 00:11:40,812
(Moomoo's Fun Run took the running scene by storm.)

334
00:11:41,452 --> 00:11:43,052
- It was shaped like a puppy. - Right.

335
00:11:43,052 --> 00:11:44,522
Will it be different today?

336
00:11:44,522 --> 00:11:45,582
It will be different today.

337
00:11:45,952 --> 00:11:47,752
I'm going to form the Fun Run Crew.

338
00:11:47,752 --> 00:11:49,422
(He decided to form a crew.)

339
00:11:49,552 --> 00:11:52,392
I picked guys who wouldn't be stressed...

340
00:11:52,392 --> 00:11:54,332
from running.

341
00:11:54,592 --> 00:11:55,662
I picked Dowoon.

342
00:11:55,662 --> 00:11:57,932
It seems he's only interested in boxing and nothing else.

343
00:11:58,132 --> 00:11:59,302
That's great.

344
00:11:59,302 --> 00:12:01,302
I welcome people who love lounging around at home.

345
00:12:01,772 --> 00:12:03,942
It looks like running will never be a regular hobby for him.

346
00:12:04,142 --> 00:12:05,272
I picked Ji Hyeon.

347
00:12:05,272 --> 00:12:07,542
(Ji Hyeon is a couch potato.)

348
00:12:07,542 --> 00:12:09,442
I chose Na Ra. He showed us a weird style of running...

349
00:12:09,442 --> 00:12:10,912
when he went camping.

350
00:12:10,912 --> 00:12:14,752
(The follower of the Fun Run, Na Ra)

351
00:12:14,752 --> 00:12:16,282
I focused on that.

352
00:12:16,282 --> 00:12:18,452
Your pace is quite fast for the Fun Run.

353
00:12:19,022 --> 00:12:20,522
I picked these three guys for the crew.

354
00:12:20,522 --> 00:12:22,392
(I thought long and hard to pick these three guys.)

355
00:12:22,392 --> 00:12:23,692
The kind-hearted trio.

356
00:12:25,492 --> 00:12:27,992
They have this desire to run.

357
00:12:28,432 --> 00:12:31,362
I'll bring out this desire from them and that's why I invited them.

358
00:12:32,062 --> 00:12:33,602
We'll start small.

359
00:12:33,602 --> 00:12:35,002
(Every history has a beginning.)

360
00:12:35,002 --> 00:12:36,232
I keep seeing this word, "history."

361
00:12:36,232 --> 00:12:38,002
(The Birth of the 1st Fun Run Crew)

362
00:12:38,002 --> 00:12:40,612
As it so happens, I read...

363
00:12:40,612 --> 00:12:43,012
this news article today that some people had finished...

364
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,442
the marathon under two hours.

365
00:12:44,442 --> 00:12:45,642
- Today? - Really?

366
00:12:45,642 --> 00:12:46,752
- Really? - Someone broke that record.

367
00:12:46,752 --> 00:12:48,212
- Really? - Two people did.

368
00:12:48,552 --> 00:12:50,382
It happened at the London Marathon?

369
00:12:50,652 --> 00:12:52,522
Finishing the marathon under two hours...

370
00:12:52,522 --> 00:12:54,222
- had been a goal for mankind. - Right.

371
00:12:54,392 --> 00:12:56,822
So this is the world we live in now. But the Fun Run...

372
00:12:56,822 --> 00:12:58,722
If you can't accomplish that,

373
00:12:58,722 --> 00:13:00,392
- our approach will be better. - It's better to have fun with it.

374
00:13:00,392 --> 00:13:01,692
- It's better to have fun. - Of course.

375
00:13:02,432 --> 00:13:04,032
Do you know why we came here?

376
00:13:04,262 --> 00:13:07,802
Do you know why we're holding our inauguration ceremony here?

377
00:13:08,432 --> 00:13:10,002
- Where's your hometown? - Mokpo.

378
00:13:10,142 --> 00:13:11,202
- It's Jeolla Province, right? - Yes.

379
00:13:11,202 --> 00:13:12,472
- What about you? - Gyeongsang Province.

380
00:13:12,472 --> 00:13:13,512
- Gyeongsang Province, right? - Yes.

381
00:13:13,512 --> 00:13:14,542
- Chungcheong Province, right? - Right.

382
00:13:14,542 --> 00:13:15,612
- I'm from Seoul. - Yes.

383
00:13:15,612 --> 00:13:16,712
Which province is missing?

384
00:13:17,042 --> 00:13:18,042
- Gangwon Province. - Gangwon Province.

385
00:13:18,042 --> 00:13:20,412
We're missing Gangwon Province. That's why we're having it here.

386
00:13:20,412 --> 00:13:21,582
(That's why the ceremony is here.)

387
00:13:21,582 --> 00:13:24,152
- There's a story to the Fun Run. - He's good at making stories.

388
00:13:24,152 --> 00:13:26,492
It's meaningful to have it here this year because 2026 is...

389
00:13:26,892 --> 00:13:28,352
the Year of Visit Gangwon.

390
00:13:29,592 --> 00:13:31,322
That's this year.

391
00:13:31,592 --> 00:13:33,862
- We're visiting it. - Yes, we are. It starts today.

392
00:13:34,232 --> 00:13:36,762
This is the first shot of our national anthem video.

393
00:13:36,762 --> 00:13:38,902
- Until the East Sea - Until the East Sea

394
00:13:38,902 --> 00:13:40,302
(The Fun Run Crew is meeting up at the Chuam Beach.)

395
00:13:40,302 --> 00:13:42,572
To celebrate the foundation of the Fun Run Crew's first batch,

396
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,742
I wanted us to receive new energy from there.

397
00:13:44,742 --> 00:13:46,372
That could help our crew be successful.

398
00:13:47,372 --> 00:13:49,912
I'll show you a lot of beautiful spots today.

399
00:13:50,312 --> 00:13:53,282
- Are you ready for the Fun Run? - Yes.

400
00:13:53,282 --> 00:13:55,482
- Should we start running now? - No.

401
00:13:55,682 --> 00:13:57,822
- I brought some food. - What's that?

402
00:13:57,822 --> 00:13:58,952
- Do you want to eat first? - My gosh.

403
00:13:58,952 --> 00:14:01,092
- You brought us food? - Yes. I heard...

404
00:14:01,092 --> 00:14:02,992
cucumbers were good before running.

405
00:14:02,992 --> 00:14:04,162
Cucumbers are great.

406
00:14:04,922 --> 00:14:06,692
- Yes. - Ji Hyeon is thoughtful like that.

407
00:14:06,692 --> 00:14:07,762
Thank you.

408
00:14:08,292 --> 00:14:09,932
It will be refreshing once you take a bite.

409
00:14:10,532 --> 00:14:12,632
(Humming)

410
00:14:13,232 --> 00:14:14,702
This is so admirable of you.

411
00:14:14,902 --> 00:14:16,772
- How diligent. You woke up early. - Right.

412
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:17,902
(They get to hydrate thanks to Ji Hyeon.)

413
00:14:17,902 --> 00:14:19,672
I was touched by his thoughtful side.

414
00:14:20,112 --> 00:14:21,442
Hold on.

415
00:14:22,442 --> 00:14:24,212
- I brought this just in case. - Okay.

416
00:14:24,412 --> 00:14:25,942
- I know this is the Fun Run. - Yes.

417
00:14:26,182 --> 00:14:29,312
I wanted us to run with a sense of unity.

418
00:14:29,482 --> 00:14:31,982
- I brought tapes for our knees. - Good.

419
00:14:31,982 --> 00:14:33,422
- Everyone came well-prepared. - We need them.

420
00:14:33,922 --> 00:14:36,192
Watching this clip makes me want to run.

421
00:14:36,252 --> 00:14:37,362
Do you want to join us?

422
00:14:37,362 --> 00:14:39,892
- Do you want to join us? - Not that. I should form my own.

423
00:14:39,892 --> 00:14:42,562
- To pursue the essence of running. - You'll form your own?

424
00:14:42,562 --> 00:14:43,732
- A legit running crew? - Yes.

425
00:14:43,732 --> 00:14:44,902
You should run with MINHO.

426
00:14:45,662 --> 00:14:46,932
- For your legit crew. - That sounds good.

427
00:14:46,932 --> 00:14:48,302
Then he's the only one who can join.

428
00:14:48,302 --> 00:14:49,632
- It's just him. - We wouldn't join his.

429
00:14:49,842 --> 00:14:52,672
If you're not happy with his Fun Run,

430
00:14:52,672 --> 00:14:55,372
I'll let you join my crew.

431
00:14:55,372 --> 00:14:57,012
A legit running crew sounds a bit daunting.

432
00:14:57,242 --> 00:14:58,582
You and I should go and get some food.

433
00:14:58,582 --> 00:14:59,952
I'll just sit in front of the beach.

434
00:14:59,952 --> 00:15:02,312
Right. Same here. Let's eat cucumbers with chogochujang.

435
00:15:02,752 --> 00:15:05,582
Actually, I know three great restaurants by the East Sea.

436
00:15:05,582 --> 00:15:07,052
They became best friends.

437
00:15:07,592 --> 00:15:09,992
(We prefer Fun Eating, not the Fun Run.)

438
00:15:09,992 --> 00:15:12,262
I want to try that. You brought them for us.

439
00:15:12,262 --> 00:15:13,532
- Hey. - Let's do it now.

440
00:15:13,532 --> 00:15:14,792
Gosh. Your legs are so white.

441
00:15:14,932 --> 00:15:15,992
- Let's do it now. - Gosh.

442
00:15:15,992 --> 00:15:17,162
Your legs are so white.

443
00:15:17,162 --> 00:15:19,162
- They're so white. - Look at his legs.

444
00:15:19,162 --> 00:15:20,702
- They're so white. - My goodness.

445
00:15:20,932 --> 00:15:22,732
- My goodness. - Look at his legs.

446
00:15:22,732 --> 00:15:23,802
- Gosh. - They're milky white.

447
00:15:23,802 --> 00:15:25,342
They're as white as milk.

448
00:15:26,202 --> 00:15:28,042
Gosh, you're wearing a lot of them.

449
00:15:28,842 --> 00:15:31,342
Hey, that looks really fancy.

450
00:15:32,242 --> 00:15:33,712
I wanted to match it with yours.

451
00:15:34,252 --> 00:15:36,552
- I see. - Why did I dress like that?

452
00:15:36,982 --> 00:15:39,322
- Right here. - Isn't that too tight, though?

453
00:15:40,052 --> 00:15:41,622
Isn't that too tight, though?

454
00:15:41,622 --> 00:15:43,052
(Tight)

455
00:15:43,622 --> 00:15:45,662
Actually, I prepared a lot for the Fun Run.

456
00:15:45,662 --> 00:15:49,292
I really thought we'd be running a lot.

457
00:15:49,632 --> 00:15:51,002
So you wore underpants.

458
00:15:52,502 --> 00:15:54,702
No, that's a typical outfit in running crews.

459
00:15:54,702 --> 00:15:56,132
- Right? - They treated you like a weirdo...

460
00:15:56,132 --> 00:15:57,672
- because it was the Fun Run. - I became a weirdo.

461
00:15:57,772 --> 00:15:59,342
- By the way... - That's a standard look.

462
00:15:59,342 --> 00:16:00,642
- Right? Thank you. - Yes.

463
00:16:00,642 --> 00:16:02,342
I could easily see his silhouette.

464
00:16:02,342 --> 00:16:04,442
He's treated like a weirdo because it's a weird running crew.

465
00:16:04,442 --> 00:16:06,852
The crew chief applied too much foundation on his face.

466
00:16:06,852 --> 00:16:08,712
The more I watch this, the angrier I'm getting.

467
00:16:08,712 --> 00:16:10,952
Why are you so angry? We didn't even start running.

468
00:16:11,222 --> 00:16:13,152
(I'll bring down the Fun Run.)

469
00:16:14,392 --> 00:16:16,092
I'll put on the tapes with utmost care.

470
00:16:16,092 --> 00:16:18,522
- That's the hairiest part. - He put it on the hairiest part.

471
00:16:19,662 --> 00:16:22,432
- I've done this a lot. - Yes.

472
00:16:23,302 --> 00:16:24,532
Stretch your legs.

473
00:16:24,532 --> 00:16:26,302
- You must have creases here. - What?

474
00:16:26,302 --> 00:16:28,002
- It means it's done properly. - That looks so gross.

475
00:16:28,002 --> 00:16:29,072
Like this.

476
00:16:29,572 --> 00:16:30,602
Did you put on sunscreen on your legs?

477
00:16:31,002 --> 00:16:32,942
No. They're just dry patches.

478
00:16:32,942 --> 00:16:34,212
You just wait until you get old.

479
00:16:34,542 --> 00:16:35,672
You get them on the most unexpected places.

480
00:16:35,672 --> 00:16:37,882
- Come on. Seriously? - Oh, gross. I didn't want to know.

481
00:16:37,882 --> 00:16:38,882
It happens, you know?

482
00:16:39,382 --> 00:16:40,412
No. You look great.

483
00:16:41,152 --> 00:16:42,552
- Thank you. - Sure.

484
00:16:42,552 --> 00:16:44,952
(Na Ra carefully puts tapes on Dowoon's and Ji Hyeon's legs too.)

485
00:16:44,952 --> 00:16:46,852
- Okay. You get it now, right? - Yes.

486
00:16:48,352 --> 00:16:49,392
It feels good.

487
00:16:49,492 --> 00:16:51,292
- It feels good? - It feels tight, right?

488
00:16:52,192 --> 00:16:53,432
Thank you.

489
00:16:53,762 --> 00:16:54,792
(Groaning)

490
00:16:56,092 --> 00:16:58,132
Oh, it's my leg hair. Darn it.

491
00:16:58,332 --> 00:16:59,902
- Will this be okay? - I'm sorry.

492
00:16:59,902 --> 00:17:02,172
- That looks gross. - You have hair on your knees too?

493
00:17:02,672 --> 00:17:03,842
By the way,

494
00:17:04,802 --> 00:17:06,742
becoming a regular member of this crew isn't easy.

495
00:17:06,872 --> 00:17:08,372
Okay. Are there rules?

496
00:17:08,672 --> 00:17:11,582
- I need to test your basic fitness. - Sure.

497
00:17:11,682 --> 00:17:13,482
- A fitness test? - A fitness test?

498
00:17:13,612 --> 00:17:15,282
You must go back to Seoul if you fail it.

499
00:17:15,282 --> 00:17:16,922
Gosh, I can't let that happen.

500
00:17:16,922 --> 00:17:18,152
But it's called the Fun Run. Why a fitness test?

501
00:17:18,152 --> 00:17:20,492
- You can pass it then. - Right. That can't happen.

502
00:17:20,492 --> 00:17:23,392
Right. We'll go to the spot for your fitness test.

503
00:17:23,392 --> 00:17:24,422
- Okay. - Yes.

504
00:17:24,662 --> 00:17:26,022
Guys, don't run.

505
00:17:26,022 --> 00:17:27,862
(They head out for the fitness test.)

506
00:17:28,962 --> 00:17:31,562
(They follow the crew chief down the stairs.)

507
00:17:31,702 --> 00:17:33,902
This is the Chotdae Rock I told you about earlier.

508
00:17:33,902 --> 00:17:35,332
- I see. - It's over there.

509
00:17:35,332 --> 00:17:36,642
- Yes, that one. - It looks like a candlestick.

510
00:17:37,072 --> 00:17:38,742
- That's so cool. - Beautiful, right?

511
00:17:38,742 --> 00:17:40,172
- The East Sea is so pretty. - Yes.

512
00:17:40,742 --> 00:17:42,212
You know what? I knew it.

513
00:17:42,542 --> 00:17:44,342
No one said we should start running.

514
00:17:44,442 --> 00:17:45,482
This is great.

515
00:17:46,082 --> 00:17:48,452
I hate over-the-top people who suggest running right away.

516
00:17:48,452 --> 00:17:49,482
Right.

517
00:17:50,552 --> 00:17:52,682
(They come down as if they're on a walk.)

518
00:17:52,752 --> 00:17:53,892
There's the restroom.

519
00:17:54,622 --> 00:17:56,122
- Do you want to go? - Yes, I need to.

520
00:17:56,122 --> 00:17:57,162
Go ahead.

521
00:17:57,762 --> 00:17:58,762
You let them do whatever they want.

522
00:17:58,992 --> 00:18:00,132
- I'll be back. - Go ahead.

523
00:18:00,132 --> 00:18:01,362
- Go on. - The restroom.

524
00:18:01,362 --> 00:18:02,562
If you need to use it, go ahead.

525
00:18:03,092 --> 00:18:04,362
He shouldn't have run.

526
00:18:05,662 --> 00:18:07,672
So not running is one of the rules?

527
00:18:07,772 --> 00:18:09,932
Right. Don't run unless it's part of the route.

528
00:18:09,932 --> 00:18:11,642
- Unless it's part of the route? - Right.

529
00:18:12,272 --> 00:18:13,542
If you need to use it, go ahead.

530
00:18:14,272 --> 00:18:16,312
- If you want food, join me then. - I want...

531
00:18:16,782 --> 00:18:18,042
If you smell food, eat.

532
00:18:18,042 --> 00:18:19,912
- You didn't even start running. - Why are you eating now?

533
00:18:19,912 --> 00:18:21,052
You started eating already?

534
00:18:21,382 --> 00:18:23,282
But it was really nice to run after some food.

535
00:18:23,682 --> 00:18:25,522
- I was so happy. - See? Ji Hyeon liked that.

536
00:18:25,652 --> 00:18:27,692
Actually, I like this run.

537
00:18:27,822 --> 00:18:30,362
- This is good, right? I like it. - I can handle it. I like it.

538
00:18:31,162 --> 00:18:32,922
- We should have some food. - Gosh.

539
00:18:33,362 --> 00:18:34,632
What's this? This looks good.

540
00:18:36,092 --> 00:18:39,132
(Tender, bouncy squid, roasted on hot stones)

541
00:18:39,132 --> 00:18:40,672
- That looks good. - You must get squid there.

542
00:18:40,672 --> 00:18:41,802
Right. That's a must.

543
00:18:41,802 --> 00:18:42,802
(Salivating)

544
00:18:43,672 --> 00:18:44,772
Try this now.

545
00:18:44,772 --> 00:18:48,042
(They have a taste under the crew chief's guidance.)

546
00:18:49,872 --> 00:18:52,482
(Munching)

547
00:18:52,482 --> 00:18:54,182
(Satisfied)

548
00:18:56,282 --> 00:18:58,752
- Dowoon should eat a lot. - Right, he should eat some.

549
00:18:58,752 --> 00:18:59,822
Dowoon.

550
00:19:00,022 --> 00:19:02,252
- We came here for a run. - Dowoon.

551
00:19:02,352 --> 00:19:03,362
Ji Hyeon.

552
00:19:03,422 --> 00:19:06,392
Please speak casually to me. Seriously.

553
00:19:06,392 --> 00:19:07,732
Then you should too.

554
00:19:07,732 --> 00:19:09,032
I'll do that then.

555
00:19:09,032 --> 00:19:10,502
I like keeping a casual vibe with my juniors.

556
00:19:10,502 --> 00:19:11,502
(Dropping the honorifics in front of the squid)

557
00:19:12,032 --> 00:19:13,472
Come. Try it.

558
00:19:13,472 --> 00:19:14,472
(Dowoon has a bite too.)

559
00:19:15,232 --> 00:19:16,772
I like this Fun Run.

560
00:19:17,502 --> 00:19:18,572
Look how happy he is.

561
00:19:21,072 --> 00:19:22,712
- Fishcakes. - I love it.

562
00:19:23,142 --> 00:19:24,282
It's on me. Have whatever you want.

563
00:19:24,282 --> 00:19:25,712
(The crew chief is buying them fishcakes.)

564
00:19:25,712 --> 00:19:28,212
You can finally see and enjoy these things when you pause.

565
00:19:28,212 --> 00:19:29,212
Exactly.

566
00:19:29,412 --> 00:19:30,822
You should be the PR guy for our crew.

567
00:19:30,822 --> 00:19:32,422
- Sure. - Great.

568
00:19:32,922 --> 00:19:34,422
(Feeling bitter)

569
00:19:35,192 --> 00:19:36,192
Let's go now.

570
00:19:36,352 --> 00:19:38,222
We should get going now. It's a running crew after all.

571
00:19:38,522 --> 00:19:40,022
When will we do the fitness test?

572
00:19:40,022 --> 00:19:41,262
We'll take a taxi.

573
00:19:42,192 --> 00:19:43,732
- A taxi? What? - That's...

574
00:19:44,602 --> 00:19:46,202
- A taxi? What? - That's...

575
00:19:47,532 --> 00:19:49,572
- What? - Why are you taking a taxi?

576
00:19:49,872 --> 00:19:51,442
- Why? What? - I have a planned route.

577
00:19:51,442 --> 00:19:53,812
- There's a route for the run. - People usually run there.

578
00:19:53,812 --> 00:19:54,842
We don't.

579
00:19:54,842 --> 00:19:56,372
Are you crazy? Why would we run there?

580
00:19:56,912 --> 00:19:58,182
You'll run today, right?

581
00:19:58,182 --> 00:19:59,242
We will.

582
00:19:59,712 --> 00:20:00,752
Okay.

583
00:20:00,752 --> 00:20:01,812
(They take a taxi to the test site.)

584
00:20:01,812 --> 00:20:03,852
(Oh, my.)

585
00:20:05,352 --> 00:20:07,852
What did you do to your wrist? Did you wear compression bandages?

586
00:20:07,852 --> 00:20:10,422
It's not that. I put on the hand massage device.

587
00:20:10,462 --> 00:20:12,392
It lasted like that for three hours.

588
00:20:13,222 --> 00:20:14,462
This will last six hours.

589
00:20:14,462 --> 00:20:16,492
- It looks like... - Pillow marks last six hours too.

590
00:20:16,492 --> 00:20:17,632
(Pitying)

591
00:20:17,632 --> 00:20:18,732
- You don't get it, right? - They last a long time.

592
00:20:20,032 --> 00:20:21,332
What year were you born?

593
00:20:23,072 --> 00:20:25,772
Weren't you born in the 80s?

594
00:20:25,772 --> 00:20:27,612
- Like 1988? - Or were you born in the 70s?

595
00:20:27,772 --> 00:20:28,942
- No, right? - What did you think?

596
00:20:28,942 --> 00:20:31,282
- Don't look it up. - Weren't you born in 1984?

597
00:20:31,282 --> 00:20:33,182
- He thought I was Kian84's age. - In 1984?

598
00:20:33,952 --> 00:20:35,982
In 1984? That makes no sense.

599
00:20:36,382 --> 00:20:37,482
- "That makes no sense." - "That makes no sense."

600
00:20:37,482 --> 00:20:38,782
- Let me explain. - Hey.

601
00:20:38,782 --> 00:20:40,892
- There's no way. - Don't look it up.

602
00:20:40,952 --> 00:20:42,452
- Then he's too young. - No. What do you think?

603
00:20:42,452 --> 00:20:43,962
Go with your gut.

604
00:20:45,992 --> 00:20:46,992
"Jun Hyun Moo's age."

605
00:20:46,992 --> 00:20:47,992
(Shocked)

606
00:20:48,932 --> 00:20:50,302
You were born in 1977?

607
00:20:51,502 --> 00:20:53,532
Really? You look so young for your age.

608
00:20:53,532 --> 00:20:55,472
- Really? Thank you. - He does look young.

609
00:20:55,472 --> 00:20:56,702
Thank you, Dowoon.

610
00:20:57,172 --> 00:20:58,272
I love you.

611
00:20:58,272 --> 00:20:59,402
(The 18-year-older guy is in a good mood.)

612
00:20:59,402 --> 00:21:00,542
It felt great.

613
00:21:01,712 --> 00:21:02,772
It felt amazing.

614
00:21:02,772 --> 00:21:03,982
(Love is riding on this taxi.)

615
00:21:03,982 --> 00:21:06,082
- Thank you. - Thank you.

616
00:21:07,212 --> 00:21:08,282
Come over here.

617
00:21:09,812 --> 00:21:11,952
The cherry blossoms aren't in bloom yet.

618
00:21:11,952 --> 00:21:14,522
Is it because it's colder here? Or did the petals already fall?

619
00:21:14,522 --> 00:21:15,852
- I think they fell. - They fell.

620
00:21:15,852 --> 00:21:16,992
It's colder here.

621
00:21:18,422 --> 00:21:19,422
(A verdant trail by the Jeoncheon River)

622
00:21:19,422 --> 00:21:20,592
This place looks beautiful too.

623
00:21:22,532 --> 00:21:24,962
So far, this is just my kind of run.

624
00:21:25,302 --> 00:21:26,802
- I guess I felt... - We should keep it going.

625
00:21:26,802 --> 00:21:28,702
- a bit of pressure about running. - I see.

626
00:21:28,702 --> 00:21:29,872
- Don't feel pressured. - Okay.

627
00:21:30,002 --> 00:21:31,172
Everyone looks so happy.

628
00:21:31,172 --> 00:21:32,172
- Right? - Yes.

629
00:21:32,942 --> 00:21:33,942
What's this place?

630
00:21:34,312 --> 00:21:36,572
- This is the test site? - We'll do the test here.

631
00:21:39,212 --> 00:21:41,652
You guys should've met up in Jamsil.

632
00:21:41,882 --> 00:21:42,982
The air is different.

633
00:21:43,722 --> 00:21:45,782
(Welcome to the park.)

634
00:21:46,522 --> 00:21:48,392
Why would we do the test here?

635
00:21:48,852 --> 00:21:50,192
He's going to test our walking ability.

636
00:21:51,022 --> 00:21:53,462
- Let's do three sets each. - Okay.

637
00:21:53,462 --> 00:21:55,192
Do three sets each.

638
00:21:56,232 --> 00:21:58,032
I wanted to know their basic level of fitness.

639
00:21:58,332 --> 00:22:00,402
I was going to change the route to a shorter one...

640
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:02,632
if some of them weren't in shape.

641
00:22:02,872 --> 00:22:05,442
- What should we start with? - Let's start with the chest press.

642
00:22:05,442 --> 00:22:06,442
- Okay. - Okay.

643
00:22:06,442 --> 00:22:07,442
Who wants to go first?

644
00:22:07,912 --> 00:22:09,342
- I'll go first. - Okay.

645
00:22:09,372 --> 00:22:10,912
My gosh. I have to pass the test.

646
00:22:10,912 --> 00:22:12,412
- Let's do 3 sets of 10 repetitions. - Okay.

647
00:22:12,412 --> 00:22:13,912
- Three sets of ten repetitions? - Ten?

648
00:22:14,582 --> 00:22:15,682
Wait. Is this the grip?

649
00:22:15,682 --> 00:22:17,652
He doesn't work out, I guess.

650
00:22:18,052 --> 00:22:19,052
That's it.

651
00:22:19,382 --> 00:22:21,152
Two, three,

652
00:22:21,152 --> 00:22:23,492
- He's good. - four. There you go.

653
00:22:23,492 --> 00:22:25,122
- Why work out the arms for running? - Five. That's it.

654
00:22:25,122 --> 00:22:28,092
Seven, eight. Your form looks good.

655
00:22:28,192 --> 00:22:29,862
Nine, ten.

656
00:22:29,862 --> 00:22:32,162
Okay. Stop. That's it. You pass.

657
00:22:32,162 --> 00:22:35,502
(You pass.)

658
00:22:36,502 --> 00:22:38,542
- Wait. He passed? - He passed.

659
00:22:38,772 --> 00:22:41,072
- He already passed? - Your form has to be good.

660
00:22:42,372 --> 00:22:44,182
(Here comes the next applicant.)

661
00:22:44,542 --> 00:22:47,312
One, two. There you go. Three.

662
00:22:47,482 --> 00:22:48,812
- Square your shoulders. - You're good.

663
00:22:49,152 --> 00:22:50,922
Nine, ten. Stop. You also pass.

664
00:22:50,922 --> 00:22:55,652
(Here's the second guy to pass, just seconds later.)

665
00:22:56,552 --> 00:22:58,092
The fitness test for the Fun Run...

666
00:22:58,822 --> 00:23:00,592
Was that really necessary?

667
00:23:01,662 --> 00:23:03,132
- Come on. - Even an elementary school kid...

668
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:04,562
can pass it.

669
00:23:05,102 --> 00:23:07,202
Age or gender wouldn't matter.

670
00:23:07,632 --> 00:23:10,642
As long as you're healthy, anyone can pass.

671
00:23:12,202 --> 00:23:13,442
The initiation test was...

672
00:23:14,312 --> 00:23:16,672
It was just a formality.

673
00:23:16,672 --> 00:23:19,012
- That's it. He was honest about it. - It's just a fancy formality.

674
00:23:20,212 --> 00:23:23,752
(The formality continues.)

675
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:26,022
(You're up next, Na Ra.)

676
00:23:26,022 --> 00:23:28,222
- Any plans to change your pants? - No.

677
00:23:28,822 --> 00:23:29,922
Let me try.

678
00:23:30,152 --> 00:23:32,492
(He sits down without changing his pants.)

679
00:23:32,862 --> 00:23:33,862
One,

680
00:23:34,462 --> 00:23:35,762
- two... - Gosh.

681
00:23:35,762 --> 00:23:38,002
- His form is nice. Great. - Yes, look at his form.

682
00:23:38,202 --> 00:23:39,232
He must work out diligently.

683
00:23:39,562 --> 00:23:41,072
Nice. It's nice and firm.

684
00:23:41,072 --> 00:23:42,202
- It's firm, right? - Yes.

685
00:23:42,232 --> 00:23:43,272
(Slapping)

686
00:23:43,702 --> 00:23:46,072
Seven, eight, nine, ten.

687
00:23:46,302 --> 00:23:47,672
Stop. You also pass.

688
00:23:48,072 --> 00:23:49,772
- It's better than not having one. - Right.

689
00:23:50,712 --> 00:23:51,812
(Taking a bite)

690
00:23:51,812 --> 00:23:52,882
What?

691
00:23:53,412 --> 00:23:54,412
What's that?

692
00:23:55,312 --> 00:23:56,682
- Hold on. - You're eating again? What?

693
00:23:56,682 --> 00:23:58,552
- Ji Hyeon brought rice balls. - Yes.

694
00:23:58,552 --> 00:24:00,322
- It had spicy octopus inside. - Okay.

695
00:24:00,322 --> 00:24:01,852
- Was it spicy octopus and pork? - Yes, spicy octopus and pork.

696
00:24:01,852 --> 00:24:03,522
- It was so good. - It was really tasty.

697
00:24:03,522 --> 00:24:05,422
People might think that you're running a full marathon.

698
00:24:05,992 --> 00:24:08,732
If you run at least 10km after all this, you have my respect.

699
00:24:08,732 --> 00:24:10,232
- I see. - Of course, we'll run.

700
00:24:10,232 --> 00:24:12,002
- If you run at least 10km. - We didn't go there to have fun.

701
00:24:12,002 --> 00:24:13,362
(I have a plan for the Fun Run.)

702
00:24:15,902 --> 00:24:16,902
It's so good.

703
00:24:16,902 --> 00:24:18,502
(Humming in approval)

704
00:24:20,002 --> 00:24:21,172
- It was so good. - It looks good.

705
00:24:21,172 --> 00:24:22,242
It does look good.

706
00:24:22,512 --> 00:24:24,542
(Salivating)

707
00:24:26,082 --> 00:24:27,112
(Humming)

708
00:24:27,612 --> 00:24:28,882
- Is it good? - The filling...

709
00:24:28,882 --> 00:24:29,882
It's so good.

710
00:24:30,252 --> 00:24:31,882
It was cold, but it was tastier.

711
00:24:31,922 --> 00:24:34,052
- Of course. - He's the octopus expert.

712
00:24:34,052 --> 00:24:35,092
He is.

713
00:24:35,122 --> 00:24:36,422
- The sauce was perfect. - You're from Mokpo.

714
00:24:36,422 --> 00:24:37,492
Yes.

715
00:24:38,292 --> 00:24:39,892
Listen while you eat.

716
00:24:39,992 --> 00:24:41,032
Okay.

717
00:24:41,532 --> 00:24:43,462
I prepared unique completion certificates.

718
00:24:43,692 --> 00:24:44,732
Like what?

719
00:24:45,002 --> 00:24:47,432
I don't give out plain completion certificates.

720
00:24:47,772 --> 00:24:49,672
- I got you practical certificates. - Practice certificates?

721
00:24:49,772 --> 00:24:51,072
Are you ready to be moved?

722
00:24:51,072 --> 00:24:52,172
- Yes. - Yes.

723
00:24:52,402 --> 00:24:53,672
I made them myself.

724
00:24:53,672 --> 00:24:54,712
Really?

725
00:24:55,572 --> 00:24:56,772
It took me four hours.

726
00:24:56,872 --> 00:24:58,142
- What? - What is it?

727
00:24:58,542 --> 00:24:59,542
Really?

728
00:24:59,782 --> 00:25:00,912
(Handing it over)

729
00:25:01,082 --> 00:25:03,082
What? A vest?

730
00:25:03,082 --> 00:25:04,322
- One, two, three. - Three.

731
00:25:04,722 --> 00:25:06,352
What? What is it?

732
00:25:06,352 --> 00:25:09,022
(What is the completion certificate Moomoo made himself?)

733
00:25:10,253 --> 00:25:12,123
(Crew chief takes out the completion certificate.)

734
00:25:12,123 --> 00:25:13,163
- What is it? - A vest?

735
00:25:13,163 --> 00:25:14,333
- One, two, three. - Three.

736
00:25:15,893 --> 00:25:18,033
- What's this? - Moo Do Ra Ji.

737
00:25:18,033 --> 00:25:19,203
(Welcome to the 1st Fun Run.)

738
00:25:19,333 --> 00:25:20,733
- Each drawing is different. - Yes.

739
00:25:20,733 --> 00:25:23,333
I drew them with love for the crew members.

740
00:25:25,203 --> 00:25:26,203
(Their eyes go wide.)

741
00:25:26,203 --> 00:25:27,243
What a nice artwork.

742
00:25:27,243 --> 00:25:29,243
I drew your face.

743
00:25:29,243 --> 00:25:30,683
Hold on. Is this me?

744
00:25:31,413 --> 00:25:32,543
Is this me?

745
00:25:32,883 --> 00:25:33,983
You recognized yourself right away.

746
00:25:34,653 --> 00:25:35,653
(Ji)

747
00:25:35,653 --> 00:25:39,523
(Ji Hyeon)

748
00:25:39,523 --> 00:25:41,223
How did you find your face right away?

749
00:25:41,512 --> 00:25:42,853
I really don't like this.

750
00:25:42,853 --> 00:25:45,123
(I really don't like this.)

751
00:25:45,123 --> 00:25:47,593
Didn't you squish his face too much?

752
00:25:47,933 --> 00:25:50,063
- That's... - His nose is a triangle.

753
00:25:50,293 --> 00:25:51,963
I laugh every time I look at it.

754
00:25:52,603 --> 00:25:55,303
My artwork is a success when the recipient gets mad.

755
00:25:55,403 --> 00:25:58,503
I'm annoyed because it resembles me a bit.

756
00:25:58,973 --> 00:26:00,273
Ji Hyeon, I'm sorry,

757
00:26:00,273 --> 00:26:01,613
- but I see the resemblance. - Right.

758
00:26:01,613 --> 00:26:03,843
- The details are the same. - That's right.

759
00:26:05,343 --> 00:26:07,613
If you don't like it, how did you find your face right away?

760
00:26:07,613 --> 00:26:09,113
Hold on. Let me take a look.

761
00:26:09,113 --> 00:26:10,313
(Let me take a proper look.)

762
00:26:10,313 --> 00:26:12,653
- Did you draw it yourself? - Yes, I did.

763
00:26:12,983 --> 00:26:14,723
- I'm touched. Seriously. - So this is me.

764
00:26:15,023 --> 00:26:16,293
This is Moo chewy cookie.

765
00:26:16,693 --> 00:26:18,123
That's my face.

766
00:26:18,393 --> 00:26:19,993
He looks like Bruce Lee with long hair.

767
00:26:19,993 --> 00:26:22,063
(Bruce Lee with long hair, Dowoon)

768
00:26:22,363 --> 00:26:24,663
What? Isn't this Ito Junji's artwork?

769
00:26:24,763 --> 00:26:25,763
Seriously.

770
00:26:26,233 --> 00:26:27,273
That's Na Ra.

771
00:26:27,273 --> 00:26:28,273
(Ghost Na Ra)

772
00:26:28,473 --> 00:26:30,533
The hardest thing to draw...

773
00:26:31,143 --> 00:26:32,403
is a handsome face.

774
00:26:33,173 --> 00:26:34,273
I bet it was hard to draw all of us.

775
00:26:34,273 --> 00:26:35,943
