00:44:45,063 --> 00:44:47,803
(Moo Do Ra Ji)

1286
00:44:48,033 --> 00:44:49,033
(Doraji)

1287
00:44:49,333 --> 00:44:52,843
(Doraji, Moo Do Ra Ji)

1288
00:44:53,303 --> 00:44:54,873
You have no choice but to sing along.

1289
00:44:54,873 --> 00:44:56,313
(Fallen for the Fun Run without realizing it)

1290
00:44:57,113 --> 00:44:59,543
(Fun Run's 1st Crew)

1291
00:44:59,683 --> 00:45:02,583
(Moo Do Ra Ji)

1292
00:45:02,583 --> 00:45:03,613
Let's go!

1293
00:45:05,183 --> 00:45:08,083
- Eodal. - Eodal.

1294
00:45:08,823 --> 00:45:10,523
The energy level is really high.

1295
00:45:10,893 --> 00:45:12,923
- That's amazing. - They're feeling great right now.

1296
00:45:13,263 --> 00:45:15,233
On the other side of the road,

1297
00:45:15,493 --> 00:45:17,233
there's a really good cold raw fish soup place.

1298
00:45:17,233 --> 00:45:19,103
- You should've told us. - It's really small.

1299
00:45:19,103 --> 00:45:21,363
- It's the smallest place. - Those places serve great food.

1300
00:45:21,363 --> 00:45:24,333
After driving in from the city,

1301
00:45:24,633 --> 00:45:26,703
you'll find Mukho Beach.

1302
00:45:26,873 --> 00:45:29,443
Take a left and park there. It will be right behind.

1303
00:45:29,643 --> 00:45:31,443
That place serves really good food.

1304
00:45:31,573 --> 00:45:32,983
Would you like to come for the second Fun Run?

1305
00:45:32,983 --> 00:45:35,253
- I don't enjoy moving. - We can't join.

1306
00:45:35,253 --> 00:45:36,413
(We don't like moving.)

1307
00:45:36,983 --> 00:45:38,783
- With a pleasant heart, - We will show you our support.

1308
00:45:38,823 --> 00:45:39,883
we will show you our support.

1309
00:45:40,253 --> 00:45:42,093
- Let's go, Fun Run! - Let's go!

1310
00:45:42,253 --> 00:45:43,393
- Yes! - Yes!

1311
00:45:44,123 --> 00:45:45,193
Just tell us where the good restaurants are.

1312
00:45:45,193 --> 00:45:46,593
(Good restaurants will be shared with the Fun Eat crew.)

1313
00:45:46,993 --> 00:45:48,433
This is a famous cafe.

1314
00:45:48,433 --> 00:45:49,833
- Really? - It's a bakery as well.

1315
00:45:51,033 --> 00:45:52,703
Would you not like to go to the famous cafe?

1316
00:45:53,303 --> 00:45:54,763
- Will we pass it? - Shall we go?

1317
00:45:54,763 --> 00:45:56,033
- Let's go right away. - Let's go.

1318
00:45:56,873 --> 00:45:58,033
As you wish. Let's vote.

1319
00:45:58,133 --> 00:45:59,773
- Let's see. - Will we go or not?

1320
00:46:00,243 --> 00:46:01,813
- Let's go! - Okay!

1321
00:46:03,673 --> 00:46:05,213
You're all laughing.

1322
00:46:05,213 --> 00:46:06,583
- We must visit a famous place. - We're laughing all the time.

1323
00:46:06,583 --> 00:46:07,643
This is part of the Fun Run.

1324
00:46:08,043 --> 00:46:10,383
- Look at all the people. - Right.

1325
00:46:10,383 --> 00:46:12,023
So they take a break every 3km.

1326
00:46:12,223 --> 00:46:13,953
That's around the 3km mark.

1327
00:46:14,283 --> 00:46:15,693
It smells amazing.

1328
00:46:15,693 --> 00:46:17,153
Right. They use good butter.

1329
00:46:20,523 --> 00:46:22,433
- The bakery! - What's going on?

1330
00:46:22,433 --> 00:46:24,533
They all went to have some bread in my opinion.

1331
00:46:24,533 --> 00:46:26,063
(The tray is filled with bread even though they ate earlier.)

1332
00:46:27,033 --> 00:46:28,873
Based on my research,

1333
00:46:28,873 --> 00:46:30,033
the whale's back side has more...

1334
00:46:30,033 --> 00:46:31,773
delicious places than the belly side.

1335
00:46:32,143 --> 00:46:34,373
So there's nothing to eat after passing the back.

1336
00:46:34,973 --> 00:46:36,573
That would be a total miss.

1337
00:46:36,573 --> 00:46:37,773
That isn't fun.

1338
00:46:38,443 --> 00:46:41,413
We must eat all we can before passing the back.

1339
00:46:42,053 --> 00:46:44,813
We must visit the places that are famous and crowded.

1340
00:46:46,723 --> 00:46:48,323
Isn't it nice to take a break in the middle?

1341
00:46:48,323 --> 00:46:50,023
- It's really nice. - Why must we run until we...

1342
00:46:50,023 --> 00:46:51,093
- smell the blood inside of us? - Right.

1343
00:46:51,093 --> 00:46:53,663
We can take a break when it's slightly exhausting.

1344
00:46:53,663 --> 00:46:55,263
- It's perfect right now. - It's perfect, isn't it?

1345
00:46:55,393 --> 00:46:56,563
We shouldn't be smelling the blood inside of us.

1346
00:46:56,563 --> 00:46:58,533
That must be bad for us, don't you think?

1347
00:46:59,903 --> 00:47:01,233
I feel great right now.

1348
00:47:01,233 --> 00:47:03,003
- Right. - Right.

1349
00:47:03,033 --> 00:47:04,673
This might be a healthier way.

1350
00:47:07,773 --> 00:47:09,243
(Eyes opening wide)

1351
00:47:09,243 --> 00:47:10,273
Hey!

1352
00:47:11,443 --> 00:47:14,043
(How is the butter?)

1353
00:47:16,552 --> 00:47:17,852
(Eyes opening wide)

1354
00:47:17,852 --> 00:47:18,922
Hey!

1355
00:47:19,852 --> 00:47:21,322
- What is it? Is it ready already? - Is it ready?

1356
00:47:21,622 --> 00:47:22,962
Gosh! It's ready.

1357
00:47:22,962 --> 00:47:24,862
- The butter is ready. - It looks like kaymak.

1358
00:47:25,292 --> 00:47:26,732
It really became a thick texture.

1359
00:47:28,032 --> 00:47:30,202
Gosh, you really ran your best.

1360
00:47:30,202 --> 00:47:32,272
- How did it become like this? - I kept shaking it.

1361
00:47:32,672 --> 00:47:33,832
The butter is ready.

1362
00:47:35,242 --> 00:47:36,872
I saw Na Ra in a different light.

1363
00:47:37,842 --> 00:47:39,572
He's a guy with a great sense of responsibility.

1364
00:47:40,542 --> 00:47:44,882
Even if he were to be an office worker,

1365
00:47:45,752 --> 00:47:47,152
I believe he would become really successful.

1366
00:47:47,252 --> 00:47:48,752
"Did you decide to start the Butter Run?"

1367
00:47:48,782 --> 00:47:52,752
"Yes. I must make some butter, Director Jun." Like this.

1368
00:47:54,662 --> 00:47:56,462
He's a great guy.

1369
00:47:57,322 --> 00:48:00,532
I would've really adored him if I were his superior.

1370
00:48:01,032 --> 00:48:02,102
That was what I thought to myself.

1371
00:48:03,232 --> 00:48:05,032
- Right. - Mine hasn't changed.

1372
00:48:05,332 --> 00:48:06,832
You have to shake it as you run.

1373
00:48:06,902 --> 00:48:09,172
It needs to be moved around, right?

1374
00:48:09,172 --> 00:48:11,372
- Right. It has to be shaken. - Okay.

1375
00:48:11,642 --> 00:48:13,512
- Okay. - Right. It has to be shaken.

1376
00:48:13,872 --> 00:48:15,482
- Nice! - It looks really good!

1377
00:48:15,782 --> 00:48:17,482
Gosh, this place is amazing.

1378
00:48:18,512 --> 00:48:19,612
- Should I squeeze out the butter? - Give it a try.

1379
00:48:19,612 --> 00:48:21,282
- I'll place it here. - Right.

1380
00:48:22,682 --> 00:48:24,952
He did a great job.

1381
00:48:26,192 --> 00:48:27,962
- I'll place it here. - We're in France right now.

1382
00:48:28,592 --> 00:48:29,922
How did it become like that?

1383
00:48:30,122 --> 00:48:31,162
It's perfect.

1384
00:48:34,462 --> 00:48:36,802
(Drooling)

1385
00:48:36,802 --> 00:48:38,032
Would you like some on top?

1386
00:48:39,702 --> 00:48:41,072
(A generous amount of handmade butter)

1387
00:48:41,072 --> 00:48:43,272
- Gosh, it's fresh butter. - This butter...

1388
00:48:43,272 --> 00:48:44,742
- It looks delicious. - Give it a try.

1389
00:48:45,142 --> 00:48:46,572
(Impressed)

1390
00:48:46,572 --> 00:48:48,012
(How is it?)

1391
00:48:48,212 --> 00:48:49,412
I feel like I'm in Montmartre right now.

1392
00:48:51,512 --> 00:48:54,512
(It's time to say, "Bonjour.")

1393
00:48:55,222 --> 00:48:56,222
Is it good?

1394
00:48:57,922 --> 00:48:59,622
- I realized why people do this. - Really?

1395
00:49:00,052 --> 00:49:01,122
- Is it good? - It's good.

1396
00:49:01,222 --> 00:49:03,062
- You should try some as well. - Go ahead.

1397
00:49:03,392 --> 00:49:04,832
You made a lot as well.

1398
00:49:05,032 --> 00:49:06,692
- Go ahead. - Give it a try.

1399
00:49:07,632 --> 00:49:09,062
- It looks good, doesn't it? - What's this one?

1400
00:49:09,202 --> 00:49:10,232
The salt bread.

1401
00:49:11,732 --> 00:49:12,902
It's good, isn't it?

1402
00:49:13,602 --> 00:49:14,602
It's good.

1403
00:49:16,902 --> 00:49:18,712
It's nice. This is really fascinating.

1404
00:49:18,712 --> 00:49:21,012
- It was really fascinating. - It looks good.

1405
00:49:22,112 --> 00:49:24,442
- You're having it properly. - Gosh, he's enjoying it.

1406
00:49:25,652 --> 00:49:27,082
- How did it taste? - It looks really good.

1407
00:49:27,082 --> 00:49:28,622
It was incredibly savory.

1408
00:49:29,522 --> 00:49:31,182
This is really nice. Gosh.

1409
00:49:31,182 --> 00:49:33,252
Didn't my saliva get on your bread?

1410
00:49:33,252 --> 00:49:35,362
- It's fine. I can eat it up. - No?

1411
00:49:35,892 --> 00:49:37,462
Hey!

1412
00:49:38,592 --> 00:49:39,892
The two got close now.

1413
00:49:39,892 --> 00:49:42,032
- They're much closer now. - They're connected now.

1414
00:49:43,102 --> 00:49:44,632
- Exercising together helps. - Right.

1415
00:49:44,632 --> 00:49:45,632
- Sweating together... - Sweating together...

1416
00:49:45,632 --> 00:49:47,272
makes people get close together.

1417
00:49:48,002 --> 00:49:49,242
(Sipping)

1418
00:49:50,302 --> 00:49:51,312
Is it good?

1419
00:49:51,312 --> 00:49:53,142
It's good. Try it with the cream.

1420
00:49:55,042 --> 00:49:57,112
(Sipping)

1421
00:49:57,242 --> 00:49:58,312
It's good.

1422
00:50:00,582 --> 00:50:02,852
I love the first crew of the Fun Run.

1423
00:50:04,282 --> 00:50:05,322
I really do.

1424
00:50:05,322 --> 00:50:06,492
(Peeking)

1425
00:50:06,752 --> 00:50:08,592
I worked with my father in the past...

1426
00:50:09,162 --> 00:50:10,492
to make some doenjang jjigae.

1427
00:50:10,962 --> 00:50:12,592
- I feel full now. - Hold on, Ji Hyeon.

1428
00:50:12,732 --> 00:50:14,092
- Thank you. - He's sweet.

1429
00:50:14,092 --> 00:50:15,832
- You're so sweet. - You're good now.

1430
00:50:17,462 --> 00:50:18,872
Shall we get going now, Hyun Moo?

1431
00:50:19,832 --> 00:50:20,902
Why leave so early?

1432
00:50:20,902 --> 00:50:22,942
(Joking)

1433
00:50:22,942 --> 00:50:24,872
- They feel a lot closer now. - Right.

1434
00:50:25,842 --> 00:50:28,512
We had a great start together.

1435
00:50:28,782 --> 00:50:30,782
The guys were all favorable.

1436
00:50:31,142 --> 00:50:33,982
If one of them showed a negative response,

1437
00:50:34,882 --> 00:50:36,022
it would've affected us.

1438
00:50:36,752 --> 00:50:39,792
But none of them said no to anything.

1439
00:50:40,292 --> 00:50:42,722
"Let's go! Sounds good!"

1440
00:50:43,362 --> 00:50:45,692
"This is fun!" They all cheered each other up.

1441
00:50:45,962 --> 00:50:49,032
It was the exact atmosphere that I wished for.

1442
00:50:49,462 --> 00:50:51,162
It's comfortable to watch as none of them seem to feel stressed out.

1443
00:50:51,162 --> 00:50:52,272
Same here.

1444
00:50:52,272 --> 00:50:53,902
- It's comfortable to watch. - It's comfortable to watch.

1445
00:50:55,042 --> 00:50:57,442
(They set off again after filling their stomachs.)

1446
00:50:57,902 --> 00:50:59,072
Uphill!

1447
00:50:59,372 --> 00:51:00,472
Uphill!

1448
00:51:01,982 --> 00:51:03,082
Uphill!

1449
00:51:04,012 --> 00:51:05,512
Are you sure you're going uphill?

1450
00:51:05,782 --> 00:51:08,952
(Embarrassed)

1451
00:51:09,952 --> 00:51:11,822
(Doraji, doraji)

1452
00:51:11,822 --> 00:51:14,252
(Moo Do Ra Ji)

1453
00:51:15,562 --> 00:51:21,032
(They manage to go uphill while singing the Moo Do Ra Ji song.)

1454
00:51:21,462 --> 00:51:22,902
When the Moo Do Ra Ji song was sung,

1455
00:51:23,302 --> 00:51:25,732
- it happened to bring up my energy. - Right.

1456
00:51:25,732 --> 00:51:28,142
- These chants are really important. - Right.

1457
00:51:28,872 --> 00:51:30,372
- Hello. - Hello.

1458
00:51:30,372 --> 00:51:31,942
- We're Moo Do Ra Ji. - Hello.

1459
00:51:34,012 --> 00:51:37,082
We're a new trot group.

1460
00:51:38,552 --> 00:51:40,212
(It's great to see you.)

1461
00:51:40,212 --> 00:51:42,022
We could get sick if we run too fast.

1462
00:51:42,622 --> 00:51:44,252
Take it easy as it might startle our bodies.

1463
00:51:44,252 --> 00:51:45,952
This is the perfect speed.

1464
00:51:48,322 --> 00:51:49,392
Let's go!

1465
00:51:52,892 --> 00:51:56,302
People might think we're finishing a 30km course.

1466
00:51:57,102 --> 00:51:58,532
People might think it's a run around the whole country.

1467
00:51:59,302 --> 00:52:00,402
Don't give up!

1468
00:52:02,042 --> 00:52:03,702
- Don't get exhausted. - Never give up.

1469
00:52:04,372 --> 00:52:06,172
- Be unbreakable. - Wear long johns?

1470
00:52:06,342 --> 00:52:07,812
Oh, "Never give up."

1471
00:52:08,382 --> 00:52:09,482
He thought he was told to wear long johns.

1472
00:52:10,442 --> 00:52:13,112
It feels like it's a full-course marathon.

1473
00:52:13,912 --> 00:52:15,182
It feels like a long course.

1474
00:52:16,822 --> 00:52:19,222
(They head to their destination as if it's a full-course marathon.)

1475
00:52:19,222 --> 00:52:21,022
- The back is being made. - Right.

1476
00:52:21,022 --> 00:52:22,722
Okay. You see the injeomi place, right?

1477
00:52:22,722 --> 00:52:24,992
- Right. - Take a right from there.

1478
00:52:24,992 --> 00:52:26,092
(Current location)

1479
00:52:27,032 --> 00:52:28,802
Which way do we go now?

1480
00:52:28,802 --> 00:52:30,102
Keep going straight.

1481
00:52:31,362 --> 00:52:32,802
(They pace forward while following the crew leader's orders.)

1482
00:52:32,802 --> 00:52:35,342
- Be careful with your joints. - Be careful with your joints.

1483
00:52:35,442 --> 00:52:36,572
Your joints.

1484
00:52:36,572 --> 00:52:37,672
(Peeking)

1485
00:52:38,242 --> 00:52:39,512
It's quite steep now.

1486
00:52:40,672 --> 00:52:41,782
It's quite steep now.

1487
00:52:42,912 --> 00:52:44,042
Pace down.

1488
00:52:44,042 --> 00:52:46,082
(A steep uphill course appears in front of Moo Do Ra Ji.)

1489
00:52:46,512 --> 00:52:47,752
- It's quite long. - It's quite long.

1490
00:52:47,752 --> 00:52:48,782
It's long.

1491
00:52:49,022 --> 00:52:51,892
The slope was around 2km long.

1492
00:52:51,892 --> 00:52:53,292
- Gosh. - Gosh, it's long.

1493
00:52:53,852 --> 00:52:55,592
The GPS doesn't show uphill courses.

1494
00:52:55,922 --> 00:52:57,362
If there were contour lines,

1495
00:52:58,562 --> 00:52:59,792
I would've taken out the head course.

1496
00:52:59,862 --> 00:53:01,962
I didn't know that the head course was this steep.

1497
00:53:02,702 --> 00:53:05,072
It was really steep.

1498
00:53:06,372 --> 00:53:09,572
This was bad judgment on my part, but we had to carry on.

1499
00:53:12,542 --> 00:53:15,242
(In front of the Fun Run crew,)

1500
00:53:16,412 --> 00:53:19,712
(a steep uphill course that doesn't look fun appears.)

1501
00:53:20,582 --> 00:53:23,482
(Panting)

1502
00:53:26,322 --> 00:53:29,062
(So Fun Runs have tough times as well.)

1503
00:53:30,092 --> 00:53:32,232
(Vivid memories of that moment)

1504
00:53:33,162 --> 00:53:35,332
(Shocking and terrifying scenes)

1505
00:53:35,802 --> 00:53:36,962
That's terrible.

1506
00:53:37,802 --> 00:53:40,302
(What happened to Moo Do Ra Ji?)

1507
00:53:40,972 --> 00:53:41,972
(I Live Alone)

1508
00:53:46,972 --> 00:53:50,112
(My Partner Forever)

1509
00:53:50,612 --> 00:53:51,852
This is going to be fun.

1510
00:53:53,382 --> 00:53:56,322
Let's have fun today. Got it?

1511
00:53:56,322 --> 00:53:58,722
(Jae Hyeon walks while talking to his bag.)

1512
00:53:58,722 --> 00:54:00,052
You're feeling good, right?

1513
00:54:01,452 --> 00:54:02,792
Do you want to take a look outside?

1514
00:54:03,362 --> 00:54:04,422
Can you see things outside?

1515
00:54:05,162 --> 00:54:06,532
- It's raining. Nice, isn't it? - Did you go outside?

1516
00:54:06,532 --> 00:54:07,932
It was a while since I went outside with Anju.

1517
00:54:07,932 --> 00:54:11,232
You're really blessed for that to happen, Jae Hyeon.

1518
00:54:11,332 --> 00:54:12,972
- Why is that? - You're blessed to have...

1519
00:54:12,972 --> 00:54:14,232
a cat that can go outside.

1520
00:54:14,232 --> 00:54:17,042
What usually happens when you take a cat outside?

1521
00:54:17,042 --> 00:54:18,872
Most cats can't be taken outside.

1522
00:54:18,872 --> 00:54:20,012
- Right. - Most of them.

1523
00:54:20,012 --> 00:54:21,842
- They hate going outside? - They usually won't stay still.

1524
00:54:21,842 --> 00:54:23,282
(They usually won't stay still.)

1525
00:54:23,482 --> 00:54:24,712
Do the wildcats in your house...

1526
00:54:24,712 --> 00:54:26,982
go wild when you take them outside?

1527
00:54:26,982 --> 00:54:29,422
- That would be the end of me. - Really?

1528
00:54:29,422 --> 00:54:30,622
- Really? - That would be the end of you?

1529
00:54:30,752 --> 00:54:32,122
It's our first time, isn't it, Anju?

1530
00:54:32,122 --> 00:54:33,722
Anju doesn't go outside often either.

1531
00:54:33,722 --> 00:54:36,422
I usually take him outside when we visit the vet.

1532
00:54:36,422 --> 00:54:37,762
He's really calm.

1533
00:54:37,762 --> 00:54:39,162
- He's really calm. - Right.

1534
00:54:40,262 --> 00:54:41,262
Let's go.

1535
00:54:42,332 --> 00:54:43,462
Let's go.

1536
00:54:43,462 --> 00:54:44,532
(He walks down to the basement.)

1537
00:54:44,532 --> 00:54:45,672
- Let's go. - Where is this?

1538
00:54:46,272 --> 00:54:47,572
