01:04:13,102 --> 01:04:14,102
He's so cute.

1797
01:04:15,172 --> 01:04:17,072
- Why is he so... - What's wrong with me?

1798
01:04:17,942 --> 01:04:19,142
My goodness.

1799
01:04:22,982 --> 01:04:23,982
(Excited)

1800
01:04:23,982 --> 01:04:25,882
He poses so well now, right?

1801
01:04:27,782 --> 01:04:28,782
(Sweaty)

1802
01:04:28,782 --> 01:04:30,252
Gosh, look at all that sweat.

1803
01:04:30,422 --> 01:04:31,522
It was tiring.

1804
01:04:31,522 --> 01:04:33,222
(It was tiring.)

1805
01:04:34,252 --> 01:04:36,192
(Dragging his tired body...)

1806
01:04:38,062 --> 01:04:39,592
This is a lot of work.

1807
01:04:40,062 --> 01:04:41,062
Ta-da.

1808
01:04:41,062 --> 01:04:44,002
(He does his best to take the first official family photo.)

1809
01:04:45,202 --> 01:04:47,332
How cute! This is crazy, Anju.

1810
01:04:49,642 --> 01:04:52,272
(A large batch of A-cuts salvaged at the end of the shoot)

1811
01:04:52,272 --> 01:04:54,012
My wish came true.

1812
01:04:54,012 --> 01:04:55,112
I was happy.

1813
01:04:55,242 --> 01:04:56,382
That's cool.

1814
01:04:56,712 --> 01:04:57,782
Wait.

1815
01:04:59,882 --> 01:05:00,952
Time's up.

1816
01:05:03,122 --> 01:05:06,192
(He gave it everything.)

1817
01:05:06,192 --> 01:05:07,952
Anju, well done.

1818
01:05:09,762 --> 01:05:12,532
(Returning to the carrier after doing a good job)

1819
01:05:12,532 --> 01:05:13,662
It was more difficult than a magazine photoshoot.

1820
01:05:15,062 --> 01:05:16,202
It's meaningful that you took photos like those.

1821
01:05:16,202 --> 01:05:17,302
- Anju. - That's right.

1822
01:05:17,502 --> 01:05:18,562
That was amazing.

1823
01:05:18,972 --> 01:05:20,902
It was fantastic.

1824
01:05:23,172 --> 01:05:25,272
I should roll off his fur with a lint roller.

1825
01:05:25,912 --> 01:05:27,542
Do you have to clean up after using the space?

1826
01:05:27,542 --> 01:05:30,812
They clean it for us, but I did it just in case.

1827
01:05:30,812 --> 01:05:32,012
Other people use it too.

1828
01:05:32,012 --> 01:05:33,152
(Just in case!)

1829
01:05:34,852 --> 01:05:38,682
(After a chaotic photoshoot...)

1830
01:05:38,782 --> 01:05:40,392
- Goodbye. - Goodbye.

1831
01:05:40,392 --> 01:05:42,192
- Great work. Thank you. - Bye.

1832
01:05:44,192 --> 01:05:45,422
(Hurrying out with his umbrella)

1833
01:05:45,422 --> 01:05:46,562
It's raining.

1834
01:05:49,032 --> 01:05:51,832
(Trudging)

1835
01:05:52,162 --> 01:05:53,232
Gosh.

1836
01:05:53,872 --> 01:05:55,332
Anju, that was fun, right?

1837
01:05:56,372 --> 01:05:58,142
You could be a model.

1838
01:05:59,612 --> 01:06:01,712
Do you want to become a cat model?

1839
01:06:01,712 --> 01:06:03,842
(Do you want to become a cat model, Anju?)

1840
01:06:03,842 --> 01:06:04,942
Let's take a taxi.

1841
01:06:04,942 --> 01:06:05,982
(I'll think about it.)

1842
01:06:06,582 --> 01:06:07,652
Are you happy?

1843
01:06:08,452 --> 01:06:09,682
The weather's good?

1844
01:06:10,552 --> 01:06:12,392
(Glancing)

1845
01:06:13,652 --> 01:06:16,122
(The taxi is here.)

1846
01:06:17,592 --> 01:06:19,392
(Let's go.)

1847
01:06:19,392 --> 01:06:21,162
- Hello. - Hello, sir.

1848
01:06:21,162 --> 01:06:23,502
Sir, it's my first time in a pet taxi.

1849
01:06:23,502 --> 01:06:24,702
- Is that so? - Yes.

1850
01:06:24,702 --> 01:06:25,772
I see.

1851
01:06:26,702 --> 01:06:28,972
It's so nice that there's a pet taxi.

1852
01:06:30,072 --> 01:06:33,442
Anju, it feels like it's been forever since we last went out.

1853
01:06:33,442 --> 01:06:34,442
(It's been a while since he and Anju went for a drive.)

1854
01:06:35,142 --> 01:06:37,482
Anju, today was so much fun, right?

1855
01:06:38,012 --> 01:06:39,052
Right?

1856
01:06:39,152 --> 01:06:40,182
Yes or no?

1857
01:06:40,512 --> 01:06:42,212
I always ask that too.

1858
01:06:42,212 --> 01:06:43,682
- Right? - They wouldn't answer, so...

1859
01:06:43,682 --> 01:06:45,182
(That's true.)

1860
01:06:45,652 --> 01:06:47,992
Don't say anything if you agree.

1861
01:06:51,122 --> 01:06:52,192
How cute.

1862
01:06:53,432 --> 01:06:55,062
Cats are the cutest in that angle.

1863
01:06:56,302 --> 01:06:57,362
Great.

1864
01:06:57,602 --> 01:06:59,602
(We're indeed meant to be.)

1865
01:07:00,002 --> 01:07:01,702
We're taking an overpass?

1866
01:07:01,702 --> 01:07:02,772
(The couple of the century is heading somewhere.)

1867
01:07:02,772 --> 01:07:05,102
The cherry blossoms have bloomed too.

1868
01:07:05,742 --> 01:07:08,442
It's been a while since we last saw cherry blossoms too.

1869
01:07:08,772 --> 01:07:10,612
You're a good cat.

1870
01:07:10,612 --> 01:07:13,512
I wonder what cats think while looking out the view.

1871
01:07:13,512 --> 01:07:14,612
Right?

1872
01:07:15,012 --> 01:07:17,822
It will be perfect if we listen to the rain and take a nap, right?

1873
01:07:19,092 --> 01:07:21,622
- It'll be perfect with jazz, right? - You talk to him a lot.

1874
01:07:21,622 --> 01:07:22,692
I should.

1875
01:07:22,692 --> 01:07:23,992
You talk to him a lot.

1876
01:07:25,122 --> 01:07:26,462
- Thank you, sir. - Sure.

1877
01:07:26,462 --> 01:07:27,632
Thank you.

1878
01:07:27,732 --> 01:07:28,832
Thank you.

1879
01:07:30,132 --> 01:07:32,062
(Grunting)

1880
01:07:33,702 --> 01:07:36,202
You slept well, didn't you, Anju?

1881
01:07:36,202 --> 01:07:37,442
(Going somewhere while asking how Anju was)

1882
01:07:37,442 --> 01:07:38,502
You slept well.

1883
01:07:40,272 --> 01:07:41,442
We're here.

1884
01:07:41,442 --> 01:07:42,442
Where are you?

1885
01:07:42,442 --> 01:07:43,612
Hello.

1886
01:07:44,312 --> 01:07:45,342
A hospital?

1887
01:07:45,342 --> 01:07:46,752
Hello.

1888
01:07:46,912 --> 01:07:49,882
It's not easy to go out with a cat.

1889
01:07:50,052 --> 01:07:51,122
- So... - That's right.

1890
01:07:51,552 --> 01:07:53,752
I tend to go out and handle all errands at once.

1891
01:07:54,592 --> 01:07:57,422
Today is Anju's health checkup day.

1892
01:07:58,062 --> 01:08:01,192
He gets a health checkup once a year,

1893
01:08:02,062 --> 01:08:03,802
but he's so old,

1894
01:08:04,032 --> 01:08:07,432
so he's going to take all the tests he can.

1895
01:08:07,432 --> 01:08:08,532
(A full-course health checkup)

1896
01:08:09,772 --> 01:08:11,642
- Hello. - Hello.

1897
01:08:12,172 --> 01:08:13,212
Oh, my.

1898
01:08:13,412 --> 01:08:15,642
There's a cat like you, Anju. Hi.

1899
01:08:15,642 --> 01:08:16,842
- Who is this, Anju? - What?

1900
01:08:16,842 --> 01:08:18,182
- Gosh, he looks like Anju. - It's Haneul.

1901
01:08:19,082 --> 01:08:20,782
How old is Haneul?

1902
01:08:20,782 --> 01:08:22,082
- He's around two. - Two?

1903
01:08:22,422 --> 01:08:23,452
- He's still a baby. - He's still a baby.

1904
01:08:23,452 --> 01:08:24,982
Haneul is so pretty.

1905
01:08:24,982 --> 01:08:26,722
(A beautiful cat)

1906
01:08:26,892 --> 01:08:28,052
You're here for Anju's health checkup, right?

1907
01:08:28,052 --> 01:08:29,822
Yes, Anju is here for his health checkup.

1908
01:08:29,822 --> 01:08:31,092
One second, please.

1909
01:08:31,092 --> 01:08:32,732
You can go into the doctor's office now.

1910
01:08:33,932 --> 01:08:36,032
- Hello, sir. - Hello.

1911
01:08:36,402 --> 01:08:38,862
- Have you been well? - Yes. Please come in.

1912
01:08:39,702 --> 01:08:40,872
Has Anju been well too?

1913
01:08:42,772 --> 01:08:44,842
(He growled every time he was at the hospital.)

1914
01:08:44,842 --> 01:08:45,912
Before...

1915
01:08:46,112 --> 01:08:47,312
He's on a diet, so...

1916
01:08:47,312 --> 01:08:48,412
I can touch his belly.

1917
01:08:48,412 --> 01:08:50,282
- That's when he was chubby. - That's right.

1918
01:08:50,842 --> 01:08:52,042
He's been doing so well.

1919
01:08:52,182 --> 01:08:54,352
Nothing's been stressing him out these days.

1920
01:08:54,352 --> 01:08:55,452
(The consultation time is here again.)

1921
01:08:55,452 --> 01:08:57,552
He's been eating well too.

1922
01:08:57,552 --> 01:09:00,092
I switched from diet pet food...

1923
01:09:00,452 --> 01:09:02,562
- to the normal one. - I see.

1924
01:09:03,292 --> 01:09:04,622
- He hates to be there. - There, there.

1925
01:09:04,622 --> 01:09:05,692
Why does he do that when he's only at the hospital?

1926
01:09:05,692 --> 01:09:06,792
You feel bad, don't you?

1927
01:09:06,932 --> 01:09:08,592
He must have bad memories regarding it.

1928
01:09:09,432 --> 01:09:11,102
Gosh, you're annoyed, aren't you?

1929
01:09:11,602 --> 01:09:12,632
You're a cutie.

1930
01:09:13,072 --> 01:09:14,972
It looks like he knows the smell of the hospital.

1931
01:09:14,972 --> 01:09:17,302
Both animals and humans don't like hospitals.

1932
01:09:17,442 --> 01:09:20,512
How are other cats like when they go to the hospital?

1933
01:09:20,772 --> 01:09:21,942
The doctors are in crisis...

1934
01:09:21,942 --> 01:09:23,312
- when my cats visit. - Really?

1935
01:09:23,412 --> 01:09:25,612
Goodness. I understand.

1936
01:09:25,612 --> 01:09:27,982
But I feel a little relieved when I see them with their doctor.

1937
01:09:27,982 --> 01:09:29,652
- Why? - Because they're active with them.

1938
01:09:30,382 --> 01:09:31,852
- The fact that they're energetic. - On the contrary?

1939
01:09:32,152 --> 01:09:33,822
Right. You feel bad when you don't see them being energetic.

1940
01:09:34,692 --> 01:09:36,292
He must be really happy.

1941
01:09:36,822 --> 01:09:38,622
- Anyhow, he's 13 now. - Right.

1942
01:09:39,132 --> 01:09:40,792
He's over 60 in human age.

1943
01:09:40,792 --> 01:09:43,502
- Right. Like he's in his 70s. - He's around that age.

1944
01:09:44,232 --> 01:09:46,802
His kidney is... Right?

1945
01:09:46,802 --> 01:09:48,972
- He's always had a problem. - Right.

1946
01:09:49,442 --> 01:09:51,902
Also, there was a howling early in the morning.

1947
01:09:51,902 --> 01:09:53,312
(He's full of worries even about small things.)

1948
01:09:53,312 --> 01:09:55,342
He must've been really gloomy.

1949
01:09:55,642 --> 01:09:57,682
- He cried a lot more. - Really?

1950
01:09:58,542 --> 01:09:59,552
But first of all...

1951
01:09:59,552 --> 01:10:02,212
There are parts I've always paid attention to.

1952
01:10:02,212 --> 01:10:03,452
His diet too.

1953
01:10:03,752 --> 01:10:05,452
There are things I've been keeping track...

1954
01:10:06,022 --> 01:10:08,922
from the first moment I saw him.

1955
01:10:10,262 --> 01:10:11,592
Half of me is worried,

1956
01:10:12,322 --> 01:10:15,132
but half of me thinks he'll be okay after seeing his condition.

1957
01:10:15,132 --> 01:10:16,302
That's what half of me feels.

1958
01:10:16,562 --> 01:10:19,202
All sorts of thoughts occurred to me.

1959
01:10:20,232 --> 01:10:21,932
He'll be okay since you did well in managing his health.

1960
01:10:21,932 --> 01:10:24,742
What kind of medical tests should Anju get today?

1961
01:10:24,742 --> 01:10:28,172
- Since he's an old cat, - Yes.

1962
01:10:28,172 --> 01:10:30,842
he'll take a general test, a pancreatitis test,

1963
01:10:30,842 --> 01:10:32,712
an early heart failure test,

1964
01:10:32,712 --> 01:10:34,912
and X-ray.

1965
01:10:34,912 --> 01:10:36,352
It really is a comprehensive checkup.

1966
01:10:36,752 --> 01:10:38,022
You're a good boy.

1967
01:10:38,382 --> 01:10:39,552
After having dinner...

1968
01:10:39,552 --> 01:10:41,022
Gosh, you don't like it.

1969
01:10:41,022 --> 01:10:42,092
After having dinner...

1970
01:10:42,092 --> 01:10:44,392
- Gosh, you don't like it. - Oh, no.

1971
01:10:44,522 --> 01:10:45,622
You don't feel good?

1972
01:10:46,292 --> 01:10:47,332
Gosh, you scared me.

1973
01:10:47,332 --> 01:10:48,662
You're like that whenever you're in the hospital.

1974
01:10:48,862 --> 01:10:49,932
You're mad.

1975
01:10:50,602 --> 01:10:51,702
He can't be happy about it.

1976
01:10:51,702 --> 01:10:53,232
Since you're hungry and angry, right?

1977
01:10:53,432 --> 01:10:54,632
It'll be over soon.

1978
01:10:54,902 --> 01:10:57,172
It'll take around 30 minutes.

1979
01:10:57,372 --> 01:10:59,072
- Then I'll wait outside. - All right.

1980
01:10:59,272 --> 01:11:00,812
- We'll be back after the exam. - Okay.

1981
01:11:02,642 --> 01:11:03,842
Let's go, Anju.

1982
01:11:03,842 --> 01:11:05,952
(Going out to test Anju)

1983
01:11:08,412 --> 01:11:12,792
(Jae Hyeon is so anxious that he can't even sit.)

1984
01:11:15,522 --> 01:11:17,022
(Meowing)

1985
01:11:17,022 --> 01:11:18,092
Gosh.

1986
01:11:18,092 --> 01:11:19,462
Goodness.

1987
01:11:20,292 --> 01:11:22,362
Let's try it first without this.

1988
01:11:22,732 --> 01:11:25,832
(Staring at the doctor's office as he's worried about Anju)

1989
01:11:26,432 --> 01:11:28,772
- It's going to sting. - Oh, no.

1990
01:11:30,072 --> 01:11:31,302
- Oh, no. - Look at his face.

1991
01:11:31,302 --> 01:11:32,302
(Not happy)

1992
01:11:32,302 --> 01:11:34,612
Gosh, you don't like it.

1993
01:11:35,072 --> 01:11:36,982
(Getting his blood tested first)

1994
01:11:37,082 --> 01:11:38,812
His blood vessels are thin too.

1995
01:11:39,142 --> 01:11:40,182
He's such a good boy.

1996
01:11:41,312 --> 01:11:42,452
Gosh, you're good.

1997
01:11:43,452 --> 01:11:44,852
But his foot is chubby.

1998
01:11:46,592 --> 01:11:49,022
The doctor says things that deserves a scratch.

1999
01:11:50,492 --> 01:11:51,562
(Stretching)

2000
01:11:51,562 --> 01:11:52,992
(Finding it cute)

2001
01:11:55,262 --> 01:11:56,302
An X-ray?

2002
01:11:56,302 --> 01:11:57,762
(Getting an X-ray next)

2003
01:11:59,672 --> 01:12:00,872
(Crying)

2004
01:12:00,932 --> 01:12:02,102
His teeth look fine.

2005
01:12:02,702 --> 01:12:04,402
They're fine compared to his age.

2006
01:12:05,442 --> 01:12:06,512
All right.

2007
01:12:06,842 --> 01:12:08,242
(Checking his eyes too)

2008
01:12:08,242 --> 01:12:09,442
They checked his eyes too?

2009
01:12:12,482 --> 01:12:14,452
He looks like the next patient waiting.

2010
01:12:14,952 --> 01:12:17,552
(The next patient who is anxiously waiting)

2011
01:12:17,552 --> 01:12:18,722
He looks even more unwell.

2012
01:12:18,822 --> 01:12:20,252
I'm worried.

2013
01:12:20,252 --> 01:12:21,722
(I'm worried.)

2014
01:12:27,432 --> 01:12:30,762
I was sitting after Anju was sent to the treatment room.

2015
01:12:30,902 --> 01:12:33,472
But that 30 minutes went by really slowly.

2016
01:12:33,472 --> 01:12:34,632
It goes by longer than you think.

2017
01:12:34,632 --> 01:12:36,742
Also, he does it without anesthesia.

2018
01:12:37,672 --> 01:12:40,842
I can hear so well how he hisses.

2019
01:12:41,012 --> 01:12:42,942
I can hear it so well.

2020
01:12:44,442 --> 01:12:48,952
(He feels heavy for no reason.)

2021
01:12:49,622 --> 01:12:51,682
It's just a mere healthy checkup.

2022
01:12:52,352 --> 01:12:53,622
But in my head, I'm sitting in front of an operating room.

2023
01:12:54,452 --> 01:12:56,092
My feeling changes just like that.

2024
01:12:56,092 --> 01:12:57,092
(It feels as if he's sitting in front of an operating room.)

2025
01:12:57,562 --> 01:12:59,062
(Clicking)

2026
01:13:00,332 --> 01:13:02,662
Gosh, I could hear that clicking sound from outside.

2027
01:13:03,662 --> 01:13:05,562
(Clicking)

2028
01:13:05,562 --> 01:13:08,002
(The doctor is checking something.)

2029
01:13:09,642 --> 01:13:11,542
He doesn't look too pleased.

2030
01:13:11,542 --> 01:13:13,812
I know. Is something wrong?

2031
01:13:13,972 --> 01:13:15,472
(Clicking)

2032
01:13:16,112 --> 01:13:17,142
(Clicking)

2033
01:13:17,642 --> 01:13:19,552
Actually, what really scared me...

2034
01:13:19,782 --> 01:13:22,182
was the clicking sound of the doctor's mouse.

2035
01:13:22,382 --> 01:13:25,082
That clicking sound...

2036
01:13:25,722 --> 01:13:27,692
It pressured me so much.

2037
01:13:29,052 --> 01:13:31,862
"What? What's he clicking so much?"

2038
01:13:32,462 --> 01:13:34,992
As old as Anju was,

2039
01:13:35,262 --> 01:13:37,802
it felt more like a warning sound.

2040
01:13:38,002 --> 01:13:39,472
I wanted to hear the result as fast as I could.

2041
01:13:39,472 --> 01:13:41,132
I wanted to hear the doctor talk.

2042
01:13:41,572 --> 01:13:43,342
- I bet you're concerned. - Right.

2043
01:13:43,972 --> 01:13:45,342
That means he needs to check various areas.

2044
01:13:45,342 --> 01:13:47,142
- Yes, that was it. - That's right.

2045
01:13:47,312 --> 01:13:49,072
- It's because he's old. - That's right.

2046
01:13:49,072 --> 01:13:50,882
It usually finishes shortly.

2047
01:13:51,187 --> 01:13:52,957
(Meanwhile, Jae Hyeon is waiting for the results of Anju's health.)

2048
01:13:53,157 --> 01:13:54,157
Come in, please.

2049
01:13:54,517 --> 01:13:56,787
- He's so ready for it. - Because you were so worried...

2050
01:13:56,927 --> 01:13:58,227
Compared to his physical stamina,

2051
01:13:58,227 --> 01:14:00,457
- He was really fast. - he's quick.

2052
01:14:00,457 --> 01:14:01,857
Be careful. Your joint will go out.

2053
01:14:02,267 --> 01:14:03,327
You're worried, right?

2054
01:14:04,727 --> 01:14:06,037
- Doctor... - It's...

2055
01:14:06,567 --> 01:14:08,297
We were only trying to look at the examination result in detail.

2056
01:14:08,297 --> 01:14:09,407
That's why it took so long.

2057
01:14:09,407 --> 01:14:11,907
It took so...

2058
01:14:12,807 --> 01:14:14,107
(How is Anju?)

2059
01:14:14,107 --> 01:14:17,007
To compare it to the result from the previous one...

2060
01:14:17,007 --> 01:14:18,507
(How is Anju?)

2061
01:14:19,577 --> 01:14:22,617
(Is Anju okay?)

2062
01:14:23,387 --> 01:14:25,047
You've managed him so well.

2063
01:14:25,047 --> 01:14:26,117
- Is that so? - Yes.

2064
01:14:26,117 --> 01:14:27,687
You've managed him so well.

2065
01:14:27,687 --> 01:14:28,787
- Is that so? - Yes.

2066
01:14:29,627 --> 01:14:31,327
Compared to others,

2067
01:14:31,327 --> 01:14:32,727
his numbers are stable.

2068
01:14:33,027 --> 01:14:34,397
- I'm glad. - He's...

2069
01:14:34,397 --> 01:14:37,527
Cats tend to hide their diseases.

2070
01:14:37,527 --> 01:14:39,467
They may look normal,

2071
01:14:39,467 --> 01:14:42,067
but the numbers could be dramatically wrong.

2072
01:14:42,367 --> 01:14:44,867
Also, there are times when serious illnesses are found.

2073
01:14:44,867 --> 01:14:46,377
For three years,

2074
01:14:46,377 --> 01:14:48,907
his numbers haven't changed much.

2075
01:14:48,907 --> 01:14:51,407
His numbers are similar to the ones from years ago.

2076
01:14:51,407 --> 01:14:53,377
So I'm relieved.

2077
01:14:53,617 --> 01:14:55,417
- You took great care of him. - I know.

2078
01:14:56,147 --> 01:14:58,217
Also, he's been on a healthy diet.

2079
01:14:59,187 --> 01:15:00,587
This is his ab definition.

2080
01:15:00,587 --> 01:15:01,857
(Moved)

2081
01:15:01,857 --> 01:15:04,027
- The definition. - He lost so much weight.

2082
01:15:05,127 --> 01:15:07,827
(2 years ago)

2083
01:15:08,457 --> 01:15:10,297
(Anju was 6kg.)

2084
01:15:10,297 --> 01:15:11,967
- He was chubby. - He should be on a diet.

2085
01:15:12,697 --> 01:15:13,737
How heavy is he now?

2086
01:15:14,197 --> 01:15:15,297
Gosh, you're good.

2087
01:15:17,267 --> 01:15:18,307
(He lost as much as 1kg.)

2088
01:15:18,307 --> 01:15:19,407
If he lost 1kg...

2089
01:15:19,407 --> 01:15:20,977
Gosh, he was on a diet?

2090
01:15:21,977 --> 01:15:25,307
Still, compared to three years ago,

2091
01:15:25,307 --> 01:15:27,047
- the numbers are similar. - Yes, you managed him well.

2092
01:15:27,547 --> 01:15:29,587
I'm so glad you managed him so well.

2093
01:15:29,847 --> 01:15:30,917
You must've felt so good.

2094
01:15:31,147 --> 01:15:33,057
But...

2095
01:15:33,057 --> 01:15:35,687
- If you look here... - He said, "But."

2096
01:15:36,027 --> 01:15:37,357
He has a lot of tartar on his teeth.

2097
01:15:37,927 --> 01:15:39,697
And his gum is overgrown.

2098
01:15:40,157 --> 01:15:41,327
(Oh, no.)

2099
01:15:41,327 --> 01:15:44,167
Didn't he show discomfort in his left eye recently?

2100
01:15:44,167 --> 01:15:45,167
He did.

2101
01:15:45,497 --> 01:15:47,567
There's a scratch on his cornea.

2102
01:15:47,737 --> 01:15:50,007
You'll need a prescription for that.

2103
01:15:50,107 --> 01:15:53,707
You'll need to put eye drops in his eyes.

2104
01:15:54,377 --> 01:15:56,507
I think he'll be good as long as his tartar is removed.

2105
01:15:56,507 --> 01:15:58,407
- You managed well. - Thank you.

2106
01:15:58,407 --> 01:15:59,447
(You managed well.)

2107
01:15:59,447 --> 01:16:02,247
(Falling)

2108
01:16:04,217 --> 01:16:05,717
I was worried outside.

2109
01:16:05,917 --> 01:16:08,687
I thought I was waiting in front of the operating room.

2110
01:16:09,487 --> 01:16:11,457
Does he need to get scaling today?

2111
01:16:11,457 --> 01:16:13,257
Yes, it'll be good if he does.

2112
01:16:13,257 --> 01:16:14,397
- All right. - Okay.

2113
01:16:16,127 --> 01:16:18,497
- Gosh, how do you do it? - How does he get one?

2114
01:16:18,767 --> 01:16:21,967
That means the doctor will get scratched a hundred times.

2115
01:16:24,167 --> 01:16:27,237
Take a look at your baby one last time.

2116
01:16:27,277 --> 01:16:30,477
- Take a look at him one last time. - Please, sir.

2117
01:16:30,477 --> 01:16:31,847
(His heart sinks.)

2118
01:16:32,077 --> 01:16:33,917
- That sounded strange. - Gosh.

2119
01:16:34,717 --> 01:16:35,747
Anju.

2120
01:16:35,817 --> 01:16:36,817
To put an eye drop.

2121
01:16:36,817 --> 01:16:38,347
The color near his eyes turned out that way because of it.

2122
01:16:38,347 --> 01:16:39,857
It looks like he put on eye makeup.

2123
01:16:40,587 --> 01:16:42,457
Let's go home after getting your teeth cleaned.

2124
01:16:42,727 --> 01:16:45,027
It's because you had a lot of Churu treats.

2125
01:16:45,257 --> 01:16:46,797
You can hang out with Haneul when you're done.

2126
01:16:47,327 --> 01:16:49,397
What do you think? Do you want to hang out with Haneul?

2127
01:16:50,397 --> 01:16:52,397
All right. Let's hang out with Haneul.

2128
01:16:52,467 --> 01:16:54,467
- How cute. - Please take good care of him.

2129
01:16:54,467 --> 01:16:55,497
(I'll be out after brushing my teeth.)

2130
01:16:55,497 --> 01:16:56,667
- He's upset. - Yes, he is.

2131
01:16:56,667 --> 01:16:58,407
He's upset. Ae Ong got upset when I took him to hospitals.

2132
01:16:58,407 --> 01:17:00,137
- They get upset. - How cute.

2133
01:17:00,377 --> 01:17:02,947
(He comes out after leaving Anju to clean his teeth.)

2134
01:17:03,877 --> 01:17:05,047
Haneul.

2135
01:17:06,577 --> 01:17:10,147
You got a healthy and old friend.

2136
01:17:11,387 --> 01:17:13,817
You got a healthy and old friend.

2137
01:17:14,357 --> 01:17:16,427
What do you say to a healthy old grandpa?

2138
01:17:17,327 --> 01:17:18,727
It has no interest in the world.

2139
01:17:18,727 --> 01:17:21,097
It must've seen so many different kinds of customers.

2140
01:17:22,227 --> 01:17:23,997
Everyone who talks to him.

2141
01:17:23,997 --> 01:17:25,627
- "Haneul." - Everyone would talk to him.

2142
01:17:25,627 --> 01:17:27,137
He'd be like, "He's like others."

2143
01:17:28,067 --> 01:17:29,707
He must be sick and tired.

2144
01:17:30,967 --> 01:17:32,007
Do you want a doll?

2145
01:17:32,007 --> 01:17:34,337
- Gosh. - He must be sick of it.

2146
01:17:34,837 --> 01:17:36,177
"A customer before did."

2147
01:17:36,307 --> 01:17:37,577
(Sorry)

2148
01:17:37,907 --> 01:17:39,817
(Laughing)

2149
01:17:39,817 --> 01:17:41,647
Gosh, I feel proud that I took good care of him.

2150
01:17:48,987 --> 01:17:52,827
The doctor said I took good care of Anju.

2151
01:17:53,057 --> 01:17:56,297
I bet those who have cats know.

2152
01:17:56,927 --> 01:17:58,697
There are many times...

2153
01:17:58,697 --> 01:18:00,867
when we spend time with each other as if we don't live together.

2154
01:18:01,567 --> 01:18:04,607
"Did you eat?" It's something like this.

2155
01:18:04,867 --> 01:18:07,507
So, it's not like I took good care of him.

2156
01:18:07,977 --> 01:18:11,507
It's that Anju lived well and put up with everything well.

2157
01:18:11,677 --> 01:18:14,177
I think that's more right.

2158
01:18:18,947 --> 01:18:20,017
Gosh, I'm happy.

2159
01:18:26,627 --> 01:18:27,627
I'm glad.

2160
01:18:27,627 --> 01:18:30,427
(I'm glad.)

2161
01:18:31,627 --> 01:18:33,337
Anju must come first before anything.

2162
01:18:33,767 --> 01:18:35,537
Yes, he does.

2163
01:18:37,407 --> 01:18:39,407
- Gosh. - Is he crying?

2164
01:18:39,407 --> 01:18:42,107
(Is he crying?)

2165
01:18:42,107 --> 01:18:44,777
- His eyes were teary. - This breed tends to.

2166
01:18:44,777 --> 01:18:46,017
He's like a human.

2167
01:18:46,017 --> 01:18:47,117
(Cute)

2168
01:18:48,777 --> 01:18:51,847
(Crying)

2169
01:18:51,917 --> 01:18:53,917
- He must hate it. - He must.

2170
01:18:53,917 --> 01:18:55,757
Even humans hate it when getting their teeth cleaned.

2171
01:18:55,757 --> 01:18:57,287
It was because it was almost time to go home.

2172
01:18:57,887 --> 01:18:59,957
(Looking gaunt)

2173
01:18:59,997 --> 01:19:00,997
Oh, no.

2174
01:19:01,197 --> 01:19:02,797
- The doctor... - The doctor is...

2175
01:19:02,797 --> 01:19:04,197
(Before and after teeth cleaning)

2176
01:19:04,197 --> 01:19:05,667
(He looks a lot gaunter.)

2177
01:19:05,697 --> 01:19:07,467
He should get his health checked up.

2178
01:19:08,437 --> 01:19:11,207
- I just noticed that he sweated. - I mean...

2179
01:19:11,207 --> 01:19:13,107
Gosh, he went through a lot.

2180
01:19:13,107 --> 01:19:15,077
- He had to go through a lot. - I'm so grateful.

2181
01:19:16,247 --> 01:19:17,847
(Looking gaunt)

2182
01:19:19,147 --> 01:19:21,317
(He's done with teeth cleaning.)

2183
01:19:21,347 --> 01:19:23,617
Goodness. Let's go.

2184
01:19:23,617 --> 01:19:24,947
He wants to send him away quickly.

2185
01:19:26,317 --> 01:19:27,387
He must've been exhausted.

2186
01:19:29,017 --> 01:19:30,887
(Growling)

2187
01:19:31,357 --> 01:19:32,497
Did you?

2188
01:19:34,097 --> 01:19:36,327
- Thank you. - Thank you, doctor.

2189
01:19:39,027 --> 01:19:41,937
Anju. Let's go home.

2190
01:19:44,967 --> 01:19:46,537
I should take my cat to the hospital once too.

2191
01:19:49,207 --> 01:19:52,547
Anju, you went through a lot.

2192
01:19:53,417 --> 01:19:54,947
It must've hurt you so much.

2193
01:19:56,447 --> 01:19:57,547
It hurt a lot, didn't it?

2194
01:19:58,387 --> 01:19:59,687
You must've felt so relieved.

2195
01:20:00,017 --> 01:20:02,387
- Totally. I was so relieved. - Right.

2196
01:20:02,387 --> 01:20:04,057
They said he was healthy, so...

2197
01:20:05,357 --> 01:20:07,227
Shall we take a nap at home?

2198
01:20:11,427 --> 01:20:13,697
(He quickly got home for Anju who must've been tired.)

2199
01:20:13,697 --> 01:20:16,207
We're home, Anju.

2200
01:20:18,667 --> 01:20:20,537
We're home, Anju.

2201
01:20:21,737 --> 01:20:23,977
Anju, well done.

2202
01:20:24,307 --> 01:20:27,017
Gosh, my baby.

2203
01:20:27,117 --> 01:20:30,117
My dear.

2204
01:20:30,147 --> 01:20:31,317
My baby.

2205
01:20:31,787 --> 01:20:33,087
Gosh, my baby.

2206
01:20:33,087 --> 01:20:34,757
- He's happy. - My gosh.

2207
01:20:34,757 --> 01:20:36,227
- It's like paradise. - Goodness.

2208
01:20:36,327 --> 01:20:37,827
- Gosh, it was hard, wasn't it? - He took it off right away.

2209
01:20:37,827 --> 01:20:38,927
He did.

2210
01:20:39,257 --> 01:20:40,797
- You're hungry, aren't you? - He's hungry.

2211
01:20:40,797 --> 01:20:41,997
He went to his bowl right away.

2212
01:20:43,067 --> 01:20:44,327
You must've been hungry.

2213
01:20:44,497 --> 01:20:46,267
- He went to his bowl. - You were hungry.

2214
01:20:46,267 --> 01:20:47,297
(Cute)

2215
01:20:48,337 --> 01:20:51,737
Anju. I know. You must've been through a lot.

2216
01:20:51,767 --> 01:20:53,637
"Give me food instead of touching me."

2217
01:20:53,777 --> 01:20:55,607
You're right. He's doing that for food.

2218
01:20:56,377 --> 01:20:58,577
Let me wash my hands and use the bathroom.

2219
01:20:59,047 --> 01:21:01,517
(Give me food before you go.)

2220
01:21:02,477 --> 01:21:04,847
Look at his face. It's like he's saying, "Should I kill him?"

2221
01:21:05,217 --> 01:21:07,287
(Sorry)

2222
01:21:08,817 --> 01:21:10,157
You must be hungry.

2223
01:21:10,157 --> 01:21:11,527
(Jae Hyeon quickly washed his hands for Anju.)

2224
01:21:12,057 --> 01:21:13,127
Anju, come here.

2225
01:21:13,627 --> 01:21:16,267
Come here. It's time for food.

2226
01:21:18,167 --> 01:21:20,637
(It's food!)

2227
01:21:20,637 --> 01:21:22,037
He must've been hungry.

2228
01:21:23,607 --> 01:21:24,967
Eat slowly.

2229
01:21:24,967 --> 01:21:26,307
(Worried)

2230
01:21:26,637 --> 01:21:30,047
You must've been hungry. Goodness.

2231
01:21:30,047 --> 01:21:31,147
(Eating in a hurry)

2232
01:21:31,677 --> 01:21:33,017
You're eating well. It's good.

2233
01:21:34,617 --> 01:21:36,917
Anju, it's good, isn't it?

2234
01:21:37,487 --> 01:21:38,487
Eat slowly.

2235
01:21:40,657 --> 01:21:42,287
(Anju eats well without lifting his head even once.)

2236
01:21:42,287 --> 01:21:43,557
He ate so excitedly.

2237
01:21:45,087 --> 01:21:47,697
You've been managing good health for three years straight.

2238
01:21:47,697 --> 01:21:48,797
(Feeling proud)

2239
01:21:49,157 --> 01:21:50,297
Anju.

2240
01:21:51,027 --> 01:21:52,867
They said you were incredible.

2241
01:21:53,737 --> 01:21:55,137
He's indeed tall.

2242
01:21:55,137 --> 01:21:57,167
(Watching Anju while stretching his long legs)

2243
01:22:00,707 --> 01:22:04,107
I think the foundation of life is eating well.

2244
01:22:04,247 --> 01:22:06,047
So seeing Anju eat well...

2245
01:22:06,647 --> 01:22:07,717
made me so happy.

2246
01:22:07,847 --> 01:22:09,547
I was so glad he ate well.

2247
01:22:09,647 --> 01:22:13,587
So it made me watch Anju eat well after a long while.

2248
01:22:14,517 --> 01:22:15,987
Healthy cat.

2249
01:22:18,327 --> 01:22:20,257
(Knocking)

2250
01:22:20,257 --> 01:22:21,527
What? Someone's here?

2251
01:22:23,267 --> 01:22:24,297
It's my food!

2252
01:22:24,927 --> 01:22:26,097
He must've ordered something.

2253
01:22:26,097 --> 01:22:27,137
Thank you.

2254
01:22:29,197 --> 01:22:30,767
(What is it?)

2255
01:22:30,767 --> 01:22:31,967
Anju.

2256
01:22:33,237 --> 01:22:34,307
My food is here.

2257
01:22:34,307 --> 01:22:35,637
(Approaching)

2258
01:22:39,917 --> 01:22:41,947
(Excited)

2259
01:22:42,217 --> 01:22:44,647
- It smells so good. - Chicken?

2260
01:22:45,117 --> 01:22:46,317
It's a chicken burger.

2261
01:22:46,317 --> 01:22:47,717
Gosh, I'm starved.

2262
01:22:48,917 --> 01:22:50,087
Gosh, it's huge.

2263
01:22:52,057 --> 01:22:55,957
(Taking a big bite after taking care of Anju)

2264
01:22:58,227 --> 01:22:59,227
(Exclaiming)

2265
01:22:59,397 --> 01:23:00,667
(Nodding)

2266
01:23:00,667 --> 01:23:01,697
It must be good.

2267
01:23:02,497 --> 01:23:03,507
It's good.

2268
01:23:04,237 --> 01:23:05,367
This is the chicken burger?

2269
01:23:07,377 --> 01:23:11,547
(His appetite came back naturally.)

2270
01:23:12,547 --> 01:23:14,017
(Skillfully deboning)

2271
01:23:14,017 --> 01:23:15,047
It looks good.

2272
01:23:15,047 --> 01:23:16,347
(Drooling)

2273
01:23:17,517 --> 01:23:18,687
I'm so full.

2274
01:23:19,987 --> 01:23:21,587
- He finished it. - You finished one?

2275
01:23:21,757 --> 01:23:22,987
I did. It was good.

2276
01:23:24,687 --> 01:23:25,787
I'm so happy.

2277
01:23:26,257 --> 01:23:27,797
Anju, let's check out the photos.

2278
01:23:30,327 --> 01:23:32,297
- The highlight of the day. - Opening!

2279
01:23:33,637 --> 01:23:35,367
(Excited)

2280
01:23:35,367 --> 01:23:36,367
Oh, my!

2281
01:23:37,407 --> 01:23:38,437
- What is it? - What is it?

2282
01:23:40,307 --> 01:23:41,507
They turned it into a keychain?

2283
01:23:41,507 --> 01:23:43,177
It's so cute. Anju. This is amazing.

2284
01:23:43,547 --> 01:23:44,947
Look. What do you think?

2285
01:23:46,477 --> 01:23:48,147
(Turning)

2286
01:23:48,717 --> 01:23:51,087
Really? Check it out after you eat.

2287
01:23:53,017 --> 01:23:54,057
Oh, my.

2288
01:23:55,387 --> 01:23:57,157
It feels different when it's printed.

2289
01:23:59,657 --> 01:24:01,657
Gosh, it's really hip.

2290
01:24:02,627 --> 01:24:05,027
(A proper family photo taken after 13 years)

2291
01:24:05,427 --> 01:24:07,297
Oh, my. Anju. Look.

2292
01:24:07,297 --> 01:24:08,737
I'm sorry when you're eating. Look, Anju.

2293
01:24:08,737 --> 01:24:09,967
(I'm sorry to bother you when you're eating, but look.)

2294
01:24:09,967 --> 01:24:11,007
Look.

2295
01:24:11,737 --> 01:24:12,907
All right.

2296
01:24:12,907 --> 01:24:14,977
(Okay. Eat first.)

2297
01:24:15,307 --> 01:24:16,507
Anju, look.

2298
01:24:16,707 --> 01:24:18,807
Look. You're being proposed. What do you think?

2299
01:24:18,807 --> 01:24:20,547
Anju. Look.

2300
01:24:20,917 --> 01:24:23,417
Anju. I chose nine photos.

2301
01:24:25,287 --> 01:24:28,017
(Uninterested)

2302
01:24:28,257 --> 01:24:29,887
Anju. Look.

2303
01:24:30,187 --> 01:24:32,427
Somehow, I feel...

2304
01:24:32,627 --> 01:24:35,157
Anju and I are one step apart.

2305
01:24:35,957 --> 01:24:38,497
When I look for him, he isn't in front of me.

2306
01:24:38,597 --> 01:24:41,337
But he's always watching me from behind.

2307
01:24:41,337 --> 01:24:42,537
(Anju always watches me from behind.)

2308
01:24:42,537 --> 01:24:45,037
That's how it felt. So...

2309
01:24:45,567 --> 01:24:46,677
It was just...

2310
01:24:47,537 --> 01:24:48,707
I wish he'll always be there for me.

2311
01:24:48,707 --> 01:24:49,847
I know.

2312
01:24:50,407 --> 01:24:53,047
I wish he'll be my friend who always welcomes me home.

2313
01:24:54,417 --> 01:24:56,647
There was a time when Anju was really young.

2314
01:24:56,647 --> 01:24:57,687
Gosh, he's so small.

2315
01:24:57,687 --> 01:25:00,287
He's a friend whom we've spent 13 years with.

2316
01:25:00,987 --> 01:25:03,357
It was a day when memories came back one by one.

2317
01:25:04,327 --> 01:25:06,527
He's a friend and a brother...

2318
01:25:07,827 --> 01:25:08,997
I love the most...

2319
01:25:09,767 --> 01:25:11,667
and a shadow who can't be separated from me.

2320
01:25:11,667 --> 01:25:13,137
(He's my shadow who's always with me.)

2321
01:25:13,367 --> 01:25:14,697
He's become my family.

2322
01:25:14,967 --> 01:25:17,167
Anju must feel the same way toward you.

2323
01:25:17,167 --> 01:25:19,537
- That's right. - Thank you so much, Ji Hyeon.

2324
01:25:20,337 --> 01:25:22,377
If I were to say something to Anju,

2325
01:25:23,507 --> 01:25:25,107
I'd tell him, "Stay with me for a long time."

2326
01:25:28,177 --> 01:25:31,887
I've shared that Ange means fairy in French.

2327
01:25:33,117 --> 01:25:34,987
Anju, you're my fairy.

2328
01:25:36,527 --> 01:25:38,987
And lastly, I love you, Anju.

2329
01:25:38,987 --> 01:25:41,597
(I love you, Anju.)

2330
01:25:43,067 --> 01:25:46,837
It's a little sad. Time goes really fast for cats and dogs.

2331
01:25:47,597 --> 01:25:49,197
You don't want to think of the next phase,

2332
01:25:49,197 --> 01:25:50,407
but you can't help it.

2333
01:25:50,467 --> 01:25:51,467
- Yes. - That's right.

2334
01:25:51,467 --> 01:25:53,277
That's why you make more memories with them.

2335
01:25:53,277 --> 01:25:56,677
I've been noticing that my cats have aged too.

2336
01:25:56,807 --> 01:25:58,747
That something's changed because they got old.

2337
01:25:58,747 --> 01:26:00,277
- You realized that. - Yes.

2338
01:26:00,277 --> 01:26:03,987
Yes. So it's somewhat sad,

2339
01:26:03,987 --> 01:26:06,457
but it's beautiful as well.

2340
01:26:06,657 --> 01:26:08,117
It's only natural.

2341
01:26:08,117 --> 01:26:10,627
(It's beautiful as well.)

2342
01:26:11,457 --> 01:26:13,727
(Exclaiming)

2343
01:26:17,467 --> 01:26:19,537
Eat well like you do now,

2344
01:26:20,997 --> 01:26:23,307
and let's go take photos again next year as well.

2345
01:26:25,437 --> 01:26:26,477
Okay?

2346
01:26:26,977 --> 01:26:29,337
(My Fairy, My Anju)

2347
01:26:29,337 --> 01:26:30,407
Well done.

2348
01:26:31,847 --> 01:26:33,347
(Next story)

2349
01:26:34,417 --> 01:26:36,617
(The first crisis that Moo Do Ra Ji faces)

2350
01:26:37,247 --> 01:26:40,487
(An endless steep slope)

2351
01:26:41,851 --> 01:26:44,621
(I almost went back home.)

2352
01:26:46,021 --> 01:26:48,291
(On top of that, they went off course.)

2353
01:26:49,091 --> 01:26:52,501
(The crew members were shaken.)

2354
01:26:53,331 --> 01:26:55,901
(That was a lurking problem for me.)

2355
01:26:55,901 --> 01:26:58,301
(I came too lightheartedly.)

2356
01:26:58,901 --> 01:27:01,071
(They'll have a dropout, which is unprecedented?)

2357
01:27:01,911 --> 01:27:03,081
(But...)

2358
01:27:03,311 --> 01:27:05,411
(The principle of Fun Run: We're one.)

2359
01:27:06,511 --> 01:27:08,351
(Not alone,)

2360
01:27:08,351 --> 01:27:10,321
(but together)

2361
01:27:11,451 --> 01:27:13,421
(They were serious about Moo Do Ra Ji.)

2362
01:27:13,921 --> 01:27:17,361
(They lifted each other up.)

2363
01:27:18,161 --> 01:27:20,631
(They revisited the meaning of friendship.)

2364
01:27:21,791 --> 01:27:22,861
We meant it.

2365
01:27:24,831 --> 01:27:27,231
(We're one team.)

2366
01:27:27,801 --> 01:27:30,171
(Together,)

2367
01:27:30,171 --> 01:27:32,101
(we don't give up.)

2368
01:27:32,101 --> 01:27:33,371
(Holding tightly)

2369
01:27:34,271 --> 01:27:37,981
(Let's Run No Matter What Happens)

2370
01:27:38,941 --> 01:27:39,951
(Breathing in)

2371
01:27:41,381 --> 01:27:42,381
(Gosh)

2372
01:27:43,151 --> 01:27:44,581
(Since he likes spicy food...)

2373
01:27:45,381 --> 01:27:47,321
(Bum June is in the middle of cooking something spicy.)

2374
01:27:48,191 --> 01:27:51,521
(YEONJUN came to see him!)

2375
01:27:52,561 --> 01:27:54,531
(YEONJUN came to help with the spring cleaning.)

2376
01:27:54,531 --> 01:27:55,631
(Putting it on)

2377
01:27:56,401 --> 01:27:58,331
(Bum June, trust me.)

2378
01:27:58,901 --> 01:28:00,371
(Let's quickly finish it and eat.)

2379
01:28:00,731 --> 01:28:02,431
(It's a piece of cake.)

2380
01:28:03,201 --> 01:28:04,371
- One, two, three. - Three.

2381
01:28:04,571 --> 01:28:05,641
Oh, dear.

2382
01:28:07,471 --> 01:28:08,571
It can't be lifted?

2383
01:28:09,271 --> 01:28:11,281
(Wait. Why wouldn't it budge?)

2384
01:28:12,241 --> 01:28:13,381
(Falling)

2385
01:28:14,251 --> 01:28:15,681
(I can only clean the floor after lifting the bed.)

2386
01:28:16,251 --> 01:28:17,881
(I'll hold it. You lift it.)

2387
01:28:18,081 --> 01:28:19,151
Do I remove it all?

2388
01:28:19,221 --> 01:28:20,221
(This is a brilliant idea!)

2389
01:28:20,221 --> 01:28:21,251
(Bright smile)

2390
01:28:21,891 --> 01:28:22,891
(What do you think?)

2391
01:28:22,891 --> 01:28:23,991
(It's good.)

2392
01:28:24,791 --> 01:28:27,131
(Two geniuses' spring cleaning)

2393
01:28:27,761 --> 01:28:28,891
(Hold on.)

2394
01:28:29,831 --> 01:28:30,831
(Falling)

2395
01:28:31,801 --> 01:28:34,201
(A difficult task even for the geniuses)

2396
01:28:34,971 --> 01:28:35,971
(Bumping)

2397
01:28:35,971 --> 01:28:36,971
(Screaming)

2398
01:28:38,141 --> 01:28:41,371
(We'll be able to finish it, won't we?)

2399
01:28:41,771 --> 01:28:42,811
Hold on.

2400
01:28:43,311 --> 01:28:44,581
(Completely drained)

2401
01:28:46,011 --> 01:28:50,251
(Dream Duo)
